104
00:07:53,008 --> 00:07:57,808
非常に声帯に悪い。喉に悪すぎるからね。やっぱ、
so it's extremely bad for your vocal cords. It's way too bad for the throat.

105
00:07:58,008 --> 00:08:00,808
うん、お酒は駄目じゃな。お酒駄目じゃな。
Yeah, alcohol is no good. Alcohol is no good.

106
00:08:01,008 --> 00:08:05,808
あの「ガハハ」って笑うとさ、あ、楽しいんだよ？楽しいから「ガハハ」って笑うんじゃけど、
When you laugh "Gahaha", well, it is fun! Because it's fun, you laugh "Gahaha", but...

107
00:08:06,008 --> 00:08:09,308
あの、あれね、喉への負担がすごいのじゃ。
that puts an incredible strain on your throat.

108
00:08:09,508 --> 00:08:13,208
面白いとね、ああ笑っちゃうんじゃけどね。うん。
When it's funny, I end up laughing like that, though. Yeah.

109
00:08:13,408 --> 00:08:18,508
なかなかね、喉がびっくりしちゃう。うん。笑い方じゃから。うん。
My throat really gets startled by it. Yeah. Because of how I laugh. Yeah.

110
00:08:20,008 --> 00:08:23,808
そう。そうなのよ。なら、
Yeah. That's how it is. So,

111
00:08:24,008 --> 00:08:29,808
あの、飲酒配信の次の日に歌枠入れたの大丈夫か？って思ってたけど、
I was thinking, "Is it really okay that I scheduled a singing stream the day after a drinking stream?", but...

112
00:08:30,008 --> 00:08:35,308
い、いけるか？わし、わしいけるか？！って思ったんだけど、うん。
I was like, "C-can I do it? Can I pull this off?!", but yeah.

113
00:08:36,008 --> 00:08:40,408
歌うか。歌うか。お主ら、歌歌うよ。歌歌うよ。今日は、
Shall I sing? Shall I sing? Everyone, I'm gonna sing! Gonna sing songs! Today,

114
00:08:40,508 --> 00:08:46,308
あ、今日歌う曲はね、あの、前回はボカロ縛りでやったんじゃけど、今回はボカロ縛りではなく、
Ah, as for the songs I'm singing today, last time I did a strictly Vocaloid setlist, but this time isn't Vocaloid-only,

115
00:08:46,408 --> 00:08:53,808
あの、いろいろ歌おうと思ってて。えっと、アニソンとかキャラソンとか、ボカロももちろん歌うんじゃけど、うん。
I plan to sing various kinds of songs. Um, like anime songs and character songs, and of course Vocaloid too, but yeah.

116
00:08:54,008 --> 00:08:59,808
なんか、前さ、Twitterでさ、なんか「30選」みたいな、
Like, a while back on Twitter, I made like a "Top 30 Picks" list...

117
00:09:00,008 --> 00:09:06,808
30選、曲30選みたいなツイートをした気がしていて、
I feel like I posted a tweet with "30 song picks" or something,

118
00:09:07,008 --> 00:09:12,508
あんな中からもね、いくつか、ね。あの、本当は歌いたい曲いっぱいあるんじゃけど、その、カラオケ？
and from that list, I picked several, too. Honestly, there are so many songs I want to sing, but with karaoke...

119
00:09:12,508 --> 00:09:20,008
今使わせていただいている、その、JOYSOUNDさんのね、あの、カラオケアプリを使わしていただいて歌枠をしてるんだけど、
Right now I'm using JOYSOUND's karaoke app to do this singing stream, but...

120
00:09:20,008 --> 00:09:27,808
その、そこに曲が入ってたやつ、入ってたやつは歌える！って思ったから、歌おうかなって思ってるのじゃ。うん。
the ones that were available there... since I can sing those, I figured I'd sing them. Yep.

121
00:09:30,508 --> 00:09:36,208
そう。なので、えー、ま、どんな曲が来るかなと楽しみにしつつ、
Yeah. So, um, while looking forward to what kind of songs will come up,

122
00:09:36,408 --> 00:09:40,808
あの、もうデビューしてちょっと経ったから、
since some time has passed since my debut,

123
00:09:41,008 --> 00:09:47,008
その、最初の頃は、例えば、あの「熱千めら」だから『サラマンダー』聴きたいかなとか、『メラ』聴きたいかなとか、
in the beginning, I thought maybe people want to hear "Salamander" because I'm Achichi Mela, or maybe "Mela"...

124
00:09:47,008 --> 00:09:53,808
あの、こういう曲がたくさんの人に喜んでもらえるかな、みたいな、割とお主らのことを考えて、
like, "Would lots of people enjoy this kind of song?", thinking quite a bit about all of you,

125
00:09:54,008 --> 00:09:59,808
うん、お主らのことを考えて、あの、どういうの喜んでくれるかなと思って結構いっぱい選んだんじゃけど、
yeah, thinking about all of you and wondering what you'd be happy with, I picked a lot of them, but...

126
00:10:00,316 --> 00:10:04,216
ちょっと、まあそろそろデビューして時間も経ってきたし
Now, quite a bit of time has passed since my debut,

127
00:10:04,416 --> 00:10:09,516
なんかわしが歌いたいのを歌うかと思って
so I thought I'd just sing whatever I feel like singing today,

128
00:10:09,616 --> 00:10:13,816
きゃ、キャラソンとか入れちゃうかと思って、ふふふふ。
and maybe even throw in some character songs and stuff, hehehe.

129
00:10:13,916 --> 00:10:18,816
ので、あの、初めて聴く曲がある方もね、もしかしたらいるかもしれないけど
So, some of you might be hearing some of these songs for the very first time,

130
00:10:18,916 --> 00:10:22,416
楽しんでいただけると嬉しいですのじゃ。
but I hope you'll enjoy them noja!

131
00:10:22,516 --> 00:10:25,216
ということで、歌枠始めるよ、主ら！
And with that, let's start the karaoke stream, my dear folks!

132
00:10:25,316 --> 00:10:28,916
始める前に、「仮面外さないのー？」
But before we start... "Aren't you going to take off your mask?"

133
00:10:29,016 --> 00:10:34,916
そうじゃよね、そうじゃよね、主ら。あのめらちゃんが可愛いお顔をお見せしながらね、見たいよね！
Right, of course you want that, my dear folks. You want to watch while Mela-chan shows you her cute face, don't you!

134
00:10:35,016 --> 00:10:39,816
主ら、もう高評価は押してくれたかのー？押してくれたー？
Have you guys already hit the like button? Did you hit it?

135
00:10:40,016 --> 00:10:45,316
もう押してくれたー？わしはいっぱい主らに高評価押してほしいんなー。
Did you already press it? I really want everyone to smash that like button.

136
00:10:45,416 --> 00:10:49,816
おーねーがーい、お願いなのじゃー！
Pleeaaase, I'm begging you noja!

137
00:10:49,916 --> 00:10:53,016
ということで、ふふふふ。歌おか！
And with that, hehehe. Shall we sing?

138
00:10:53,016 --> 00:10:56,516
歌っていっくのじゃー！移動ー！
Let's get right into singing noja! Transition!

139
00:11:00,816 --> 00:11:05,816
あ、こっちにない。のじゃーー
Ah, it's not here. Nojaaa...

140
00:11:06,516 --> 00:11:10,516
のじゃーーー、んー？
Nojaaa... Huh?

141
00:11:10,516 --> 00:11:14,816
待ってね。わしどうやってイラスト...入れたんだっけ？
Wait a sec. How did I put that in again?

142
00:11:15,016 --> 00:11:19,416
んーー、んーー...
Hmm, hmm...

143
00:11:19,416 --> 00:11:23,216
ちょっと待ってね。一回戻っていい？ふふふふ
Hold on just a second. Can I go back for a moment? Hehehe.

144
00:11:23,216 --> 00:11:29,816
ちょっと待ってね。えーっとえっとえっと、コメントを出したくて、コメントをどうやって出していたか思い出したくて...
Wait a moment. Uh, uh, uh, I want to show the comments, so I'm trying to remember how I displayed them...

145
00:11:29,816 --> 00:11:31,916
これコピーすればいいのか。コピー！
Ah, I can just copy this! Copy!

146
00:11:31,916 --> 00:11:33,416
移動ー！
Transition!

147
00:11:33,416 --> 00:11:37,016
えーっとえっとえっとえっとえっと...これ、ペースト！
Uh, uh, uh, uh, uh... and here, paste!

148
00:11:37,016 --> 00:11:40,016
これ！できたー！
There! Done!

149
00:11:40,516 --> 00:11:42,516
よしっ！
All right!

150
00:11:42,516 --> 00:11:46,516
できたんじゃない？歌枠始められる！
Isn't it all set? Now we can start the singing stream!

151
00:11:46,516 --> 00:11:52,816
よし！それでは、歌枠始めます！今回のセトリもPNGで押し通して参りました！
All right! And now, let's begin the singing stream! Once again, I've powered through with PNGs for today's setlist!

152
00:11:53,016 --> 00:11:57,816
くふふふ、PNGで用意してきましたのじゃー！
Khehehe, I prepared it all with PNGs noja!

153
00:11:58,016 --> 00:12:00,016
よいしょ。それでは...
Up we go. And now...

154
00:12:00,016 --> 00:12:03,816
あ、あ、あ、あ、あ、あ、あ、あ、あ。
Ah, ah, ah, ah, ah, ah, ah, ah, ah.

155
00:12:03,816 --> 00:12:07,416
エコーをかけつつ...のじゃー！
Turning on the echo... noja!

156
00:12:07,416 --> 00:12:10,416
エコーかかってるー？
Is the echo working?

157
00:12:11,016 --> 00:12:14,316
主ら、エコーかかってるー？
Folks, is the echo on?

158
00:12:14,516 --> 00:12:16,416
どうー？
How does it sound?

159
00:12:16,516 --> 00:12:21,016
よいしょ。ん？よいしょ。うん。
Up we go. Hm? There we go. Yep.

160
00:12:21,816 --> 00:12:25,516
始めていきますのじゃー！
Here we go noja!

161
00:12:25,516 --> 00:12:29,816
それでは、1曲目...
Now then, for the first song...

162
00:12:29,816 --> 00:12:37,516
えー、「カワキヲアメク」って曲を歌います！歌いますのじゃ。
Um, I'll be singing the song "Kawaki wo Ameku"! I shall sing it noja.

163
00:12:38,016 --> 00:12:44,016
えーっと、えーっと...あっ、マイクがない！
Let's see, let's see... Ah, there's no mic!

164
00:12:44,216 --> 00:12:46,916
あ、くふふふふふ...
Ah, kfufufufu...

165
00:12:46,916 --> 00:12:49,216
へっ、来た！マイク来た！
Heh, it's here! The mic is here!

166
00:12:49,216 --> 00:12:53,016
よし！行くのじゃー！よいしょ。
All right! Here we go noja! Alrighty.

167
00:12:54,016 --> 00:12:57,016
行けるか？
Is it working?

168
00:12:58,516 --> 00:13:00,516
行けた！
It's working!

169
00:13:04,816 --> 00:13:07,816
トゥルルン〜
Tururun~

170
00:13:09,316 --> 00:13:14,016
未熟 無ジョウ されど
Immature, heartless, yet

171
00:13:14,516 --> 00:13:22,016
美しくあれ
remain beautiful

172
00:13:25,516 --> 00:13:29,016
てーてててて てれててて
Te-tete-tete, teretete

173
00:13:29,816 --> 00:13:33,216
No destiny ふさわしく無い
No destiny, this doesn't suit me

174
00:13:33,216 --> 00:13:36,516
こんなんじゃきっと物足りない くらい語っとけばうまくいく
If I just spout that "this just isn't enough," things go smoothly

175
00:13:36,516 --> 00:13:41,816
物 金 愛 言 もう自己顕示飽きた
Things, money, love, words—I'm sick of showing off

176
00:13:44,516 --> 00:13:48,316
既視感 何がそんな不満なんだ？
Déjà vu, what are you so dissatisfied with?

177
00:13:48,316 --> 00:13:52,216
散々ワガママ語っといて これ以上他に何がいる？
After going on and on so selfishly, what else do you even need?

178
00:13:52,216 --> 00:13:57,216
そんなところも割と嫌いじゃ無い
Even that part of you, I don't really hate

179
00:13:59,016 --> 00:14:03,216
もう「聞き飽きたんだよ そのセリフ」
"I'm sick of hearing those lines already."

180
00:14:03,216 --> 00:14:06,516
中途半端だけは嫌
Anything half-assed is what I hate

181
00:14:06,516 --> 00:14:10,016
もういい ああしてこうして言ってたって
Enough already, even if you tell me "do this, do that"

182
00:14:10,016 --> 00:14:13,216
愛して どうして？ 言われたって
Even if you say "love me, why won't you?"

183
00:14:13,216 --> 00:14:17,016
遊びだけなら簡単で 真剣交渉無茶苦茶で
Just playing around is easy, but serious talks are a mess

184
00:14:17,016 --> 00:14:21,016
思いもしない 軽い言葉 何度使い古すのか？
These thoughtless, shallow words, how many times will you wear them out?

185
00:14:21,016 --> 00:14:24,416
どうせ 期待してたんだ出来レースでも
Either way, I want to keep expecting things, even if it's a fixed race

186
00:14:24,416 --> 00:14:28,016
引用だらけのフレーズも 踵持ち上がる
Even phrases full of quotes, my heels lift up

187
00:14:28,016 --> 00:14:30,816
言葉タブーにして
Turn those words into taboos

188
00:14:30,816 --> 00:14:35,516
空気を読んだ雨降らないでよ
Don't let the rain fall just by reading the room

189
00:14:35,516 --> 00:14:41,516
たったらったら たらったら
Tattara ttara, tarattara

190
00:14:42,016 --> 00:14:44,816
そう、ドメカノの曲！
Right, the Domestic Girlfriend song!

191
00:14:47,516 --> 00:14:54,516
まどろっこしい話は嫌
I hate roundabout talks

192
00:14:55,216 --> 00:15:00,016
必要最低限でいい 2文字以内でどうぞ
Just the bare minimum is fine, keep it under two characters, please

193
00:15:00,024 --> 00:15:01,324
2文字以内でどうぞ
Just give it to me in two words or less.

194
00:15:02,124 --> 00:15:05,124
紅の蝶は
The crimson butterfly...

195
00:15:05,374 --> 00:15:08,924
何のメールも送らない
...sends no texts at all.

196
00:15:09,574 --> 00:15:12,624
脆い扇子広げる
Unfolding a fragile folding fan,

197
00:15:12,774 --> 00:15:16,424
その方が魅力的でしょう
wouldn't that make me more charming?

198
00:15:16,824 --> 00:15:19,924
迷いで応えられないなら ほっといてくれ
If you can't answer from hesitation, leave me alone.

199
00:15:20,124 --> 00:15:22,024
迷えるくらいなら 去っといてくれ
If you're going to waver that much, just walk away.

200
00:15:22,124 --> 00:15:24,324
肝心なとこは筒抜けで
Leaking through where it matters most,

201
00:15:24,424 --> 00:15:26,524
安心だけはさせられるような
while offering just enough to bring peace of mind,

202
00:15:26,624 --> 00:15:30,924
甘い雨が降れば 傘も差したくなるだろう？
if sweet rain falls, you'd want to put up an umbrella too, wouldn't you?

203
00:15:31,074 --> 00:15:34,224
このまま 期待したままでよかった
I was fine staying full of expectations like this.

204
00:15:34,274 --> 00:15:37,374
目を瞑った 変えたかった 大人ぶった
I closed my eyes. I wanted to change. I acted like a grown-up.

205
00:15:37,424 --> 00:15:40,824
無くした 巻き戻せなかった
I lost it. I couldn't rewind time.

206
00:15:41,024 --> 00:15:44,224
今 雨 止まないで
Rain, don't stop now.

207
00:15:44,324 --> 00:15:45,824
コピー、
Copy,

208
00:15:47,324 --> 00:15:48,824
ペースト、
paste,

209
00:15:49,724 --> 00:15:51,224
デリート
delete,

210
00:15:51,324 --> 00:15:53,324
その繰り返し
over and over again.

211
00:15:54,924 --> 00:15:57,624
吸って、吐いた
Inhaled, exhaled.

212
00:15:57,724 --> 00:16:00,624
だから
That's why...

213
00:16:02,124 --> 00:16:06,524
それでもいいからさ 此処いたいよ
Even so, I don't care, I just want to be here.

214
00:16:06,674 --> 00:16:08,524
もういい あしてこうして言ってたって
Even if they kept saying do this and that,

215
00:16:08,574 --> 00:16:10,524
愛して どうして？ 言われたって
even if I'm asked, "Why love me?"

216
00:16:10,574 --> 00:16:12,324
遊びだけなら簡単で
It'd be so easy if it were just playing around,

217
00:16:12,374 --> 00:16:14,324
真剣交渉 支離滅裂で
but serious negotiations fall completely apart.

218
00:16:14,374 --> 00:16:19,824
思いもしない重い真実(うそ)は タブーにしなくちゃな
Unthinkable, heavy truths have to be made taboo, right?

219
00:16:20,024 --> 00:16:23,524
きっと 期待してたんだ 出来レースでも
Surely I had expectations, even if it was a rigged game.

220
00:16:23,574 --> 00:16:28,024
公式通りのフレーズも 踵上がる癖もう終わりにして
Putting an end to textbook phrases and the habit of pitching higher,

221
00:16:28,074 --> 00:16:29,624
もう終わりにして
let's put an end to it.

222
00:16:29,674 --> 00:16:34,924
空気を読んだ 空晴れないでよ
Don't clear up, sky, while reading the room.

223
00:16:56,324 --> 00:17:04,624
Ah...

224
00:17:06,224 --> 00:17:08,624
今日も 雨
Rain again today.

225
00:17:08,724 --> 00:17:16,824
傘を閉じて 濡れて帰ろうよ
Let's close our umbrellas and head home soaking wet.

226
00:17:19,824 --> 00:17:23,624
泣いちゃうわ〜！
I'm gonna cry~!

227
00:17:24,024 --> 00:17:28,824
『カワキヲアメク』でしたのじゃ〜！
That was "Kawaki wo Ameku"!

228
00:17:29,824 --> 00:17:32,424
なんか この曲さー
You know, this song...

229
00:17:32,524 --> 00:17:34,024
あのー
Um...

230
00:17:35,324 --> 00:17:37,024
確か
If I recall,

231
00:17:37,224 --> 00:17:40,424
出たて？リリースしたての時に
right when it came out, right after its release,

232
00:17:40,724 --> 00:17:43,724
Twitterで めちゃくちゃバズってて
it went crazy viral on Twitter.

233
00:17:44,224 --> 00:17:47,324
Twitterで知ったんじゃけどね
I actually discovered it through Twitter, you see.

234
00:17:48,324 --> 00:17:50,024
曲だけで
Just by the song alone...

235
00:17:50,124 --> 00:17:52,524
曲だけで 好きになる
Just the song alone makes you fall in love with it.

236
00:17:53,624 --> 00:17:57,924
めちゃくちゃかっこいい曲。めちゃくちゃ引き込まれる曲でね
It's super cool, and it just totally draws you in.

237
00:17:58,024 --> 00:18:00,224
すごい好きなんじゃ
I love it so much.

238
00:18:00,624 --> 00:18:02,824
うん、すごい好き
Yeah, I really love it.

239
00:18:03,424 --> 00:18:06,024
だから 歌っちゃった
That's why I went ahead and sang it.

240
00:18:06,124 --> 00:18:08,524
すごい好きな曲なんじゃ
It's a song I really love.

241
00:18:08,624 --> 00:18:09,524
うん
Yeah.

242
00:18:10,024 --> 00:18:12,724
そう、美波さん。美波さん
Yeah, Minami-san. Minami-san.

243
00:18:13,024 --> 00:18:16,824
なんか、そう、この曲で美波さん知って
Yeah, so I learned about Minami-san through this song,

244
00:18:17,024 --> 00:18:18,524
あのー
and um...

245
00:18:19,424 --> 00:18:22,324
なんか 近い時期に
around that same time,

246
00:18:22,424 --> 00:18:27,724
『ライラック』？って曲？美波さんのね、『ライラック』って曲を聞いてね、それもね すごい好きになった
I listened to another song of hers called "Lilac", and fell totally in love with that one too.

247
00:18:27,824 --> 00:18:29,624
覚えあり
I remember that clearly.

248
00:18:30,024 --> 00:18:31,024
そう
Yeah.

249
00:18:31,124 --> 00:18:33,224
そうなんじゃ。漫画だけ知ってた？
That's right. You only knew the manga?

250
00:18:33,424 --> 00:18:37,424
やっぱ あの、アニソンとかをね、いろんな知る経緯があるのがいいよね
It's really nice how there are so many different ways to discover anime songs.

251
00:18:37,624 --> 00:18:39,024
曲から...
Starting from the song...

252
00:18:39,124 --> 00:18:43,724
わしは曲から、「あ、これアニソンだったんだ」って知るタイプが多いんじゃけど
I'm often the type who hears a song first and goes, "Oh, this was an anime song!"

253
00:18:43,824 --> 00:18:49,724
アニメで 聴いたことあった、みたいな。とか、アニメのCMとかで聴いたことあった、みたいな
Or like, "I've heard this in an anime," or "I heard this in an anime commercial."

254
00:18:49,824 --> 00:18:50,524
うん
Yeah.

255
00:18:50,724 --> 00:18:53,624
そういうのも多くてね、好きなんじゃ
There are a lot like that for me, so I like them.

256
00:18:53,724 --> 00:18:59,024
とか、アニソンとかはね、キャラソンとかは特にね、その作品をね
And with anime songs, especially character songs,

257
00:18:59,124 --> 00:19:02,424
知ってると、より楽しめる、みたいなさ。そういうのがあって
when you know the series, you can enjoy them even more. There's that aspect to it.

258
00:19:02,724 --> 00:19:06,024
その より深まるからさ、わしはそういうのも面白いなって思ってるのじゃ
It deepens your appreciation, so I find that really fascinating too.

259
00:19:06,324 --> 00:19:08,524
アニソンだけ知ってるのもある？
There are some where you only know the anime song?

260
00:19:08,624 --> 00:19:10,524
え、わしは それがすっごい多い！
Honestly, I have so many of those!

261
00:19:10,624 --> 00:19:16,024
アニメは見てないけど曲だけ知ってる、みたいなのが すっごく多いのじゃ
There are tons where I haven't watched the anime, but I know the song!

262
00:19:16,224 --> 00:19:18,024
そう、すっごく多い
Yeah, really a lot.

263
00:19:18,324 --> 00:19:19,324
うん
Mmhmm.

264
00:19:19,424 --> 00:19:23,724
ね、入り口いっぱいあると たくさんの人に曲を聴いてもらえるし
Having so many entry points means a lot more people get to hear the song,

265
00:19:23,824 --> 00:19:26,524
いろんな人が知れるからいいよね。いいなって思うのじゃ
and all kinds of people discover it, which is wonderful. I think it's great.

266
00:19:26,924 --> 00:19:29,824
そして、次の曲はこちらー！
And now, here is the next song!

267
00:19:30,824 --> 00:19:32,424
これはー
This one is...

268
00:19:32,624 --> 00:19:37,324
あのさ、というかさ、わしさー 音ゲーのさー 話したよね
Wait, before that, remember how I was talking about rhythm games earlier?

269
00:19:38,824 --> 00:19:42,824
『ステラ』歌おうかなーって思うんじゃけど...
I was thinking of singing "Stella", but...

270
00:19:43,724 --> 00:19:45,324
あのー
Um...

271
00:19:47,824 --> 00:19:49,824
わし...
I...

272
00:19:50,824 --> 00:19:52,324
あれ？
Wait, huh?

273
00:19:52,524 --> 00:19:53,624
どこだ？
Where is it?

274
00:19:53,924 --> 00:19:55,324
どこだ？ステラ
Where is it? Stella...

275
00:19:55,424 --> 00:19:56,824
え？待って
Huh? Wait...

276
00:19:57,024 --> 00:19:58,724
ちょっと待ってね
Hold on a second.

277
00:19:58,824 --> 00:20:00,024
ちょっと待ってね
Wait just a second...

278
00:20:01,812 --> 00:20:02,852
ちょっと待ってね
Wait a second...

279
00:20:03,132 --> 00:20:03,832
おや？
Huh?

280
00:20:04,812 --> 00:20:05,812
おやおや？
What's this?

281
00:20:06,212 --> 00:20:08,932
待って、わし、え、カラオケないことある？
Wait, could it be... wait, is there no karaoke track for it?

282
00:20:09,212 --> 00:20:11,232
ごめん、確認、確認しないで入れた
Sorry, I... I put it on without checking!

283
00:20:11,382 --> 00:20:13,532
確認しないで入れたのです、が...
I put it on without checking, but...

284
00:20:15,032 --> 00:20:16,532
ないかも！
It might not be there!

285
00:20:16,832 --> 00:20:17,882
まずい！
Uh-oh!

286
00:20:18,032 --> 00:20:19,832
まずいまずいまずい！
Bad bad bad!

287
00:20:20,932 --> 00:20:21,832
な、な...
I-It's...

288
00:20:22,132 --> 00:20:25,632
のじゃあああああ！
Nojaaahhhhh!

289
00:20:25,832 --> 00:20:27,432
まずい！
This is bad!

290
00:20:27,832 --> 00:20:30,182
絶対あるやろと思って入れたら...
I put it in thinking it would definitely be there, but...

291
00:20:30,482 --> 00:20:33,332
え？嘘、嘘じゃろ？ちょちょちょちょいちょいちょいちょい
Eh? No way, for real?! Wait-wait-wait-wait-wait...

292
00:20:33,482 --> 00:20:34,832
な、ない？
I-It's not here?

293
00:20:35,832 --> 00:20:39,532
わしが使っているカラオケアプリに
Could it be that the karaoke app I'm using...

294
00:20:39,832 --> 00:20:44,232
入っていない可能性...
...doesn't have it?!

295
00:20:46,232 --> 00:20:48,532
の... ちょ、あのさ、
No... Wait, hey...

296
00:20:49,232 --> 00:20:53,632
こ、今度歌わして。あの、ちゃんとカラオケ探してくるから。
L-Let me sing it next time! I'll properly find a karaoke track for it!

297
00:20:53,632 --> 00:20:56,632
カラオケ、カラオケ探してくるから！カラオケ探してくるから！ちょちょちょ
I'll find a karaoke track! I'll go find one! Wait, wait...

298
00:20:56,832 --> 00:21:00,032
なか、無かったことにして！ちょっと待ってほしいのじゃ！
P-Pretend this never happened! Just give me a second!

299
00:21:00,432 --> 00:21:03,332
え、どうしよう。えっと... えっと...
Uh, what should I do? Um... um...

300
00:21:04,032 --> 00:21:06,932
でもPNG、PNGにしてきちゃったから...
But I made the setlist as a PNG image...

301
00:21:07,032 --> 00:21:09,032
ちょ、一旦わしで隠して...
Wait, let me cover it with my face for now...

302
00:21:09,732 --> 00:21:11,432
え？わしで隠しても意味ない。
Eh? Covering it with myself won't help!

303
00:21:12,632 --> 00:21:15,532
はっ！ちょ、え、お主らさ、
Ah! Wait, um, everyone...

304
00:21:15,632 --> 00:21:18,932
お主ら、今一瞬だけ画面見ないでもらうことできる？
Could you all not look at the screen for just a second?

305
00:21:19,132 --> 00:21:24,032
あのさ、今、今見てるお主らさ、あの、わしPNGで持ってきちゃったからさ、
You see, to everyone watching right now, I brought the setlist in as a PNG...

306
00:21:24,332 --> 00:21:27,732
あの、そこだけ消すができなくてさ。あの、
So I can't erase just that part. Um...

307
00:21:28,032 --> 00:21:30,932
ちょ、一瞬さ、目瞑ってもらっていい？
Could you close your eyes for just a second?

308
00:21:31,032 --> 00:21:32,832
あの、セトリ全部バレちゃう。
Otherwise the whole setlist will be spoiled!

309
00:21:32,832 --> 00:21:36,232
セトリ全部バレちゃうから、一瞬お主ら目瞑ってもらっていい？
The whole setlist will be spoiled, so could you guys close your eyes for a moment?

310
00:21:36,632 --> 00:21:38,932
行くよ？瞑っててね！行くよ！
Ready? Keep them closed! Here I go!

311
00:21:39,032 --> 00:21:40,432
ステラあった？
Was Stella there?

312
00:21:40,532 --> 00:21:43,132
わしが使ってるアプリにはね、なかったんだよね。
It wasn't in the app I'm using, you see.

313
00:21:43,632 --> 00:21:44,832
な...
Is...

314
00:21:44,932 --> 00:21:48,332
え、ちょ、もう一回見るか。気のせいだったらいやだからな。
Wait, let me check one more time. It'd suck if I just missed it.

315
00:21:48,832 --> 00:21:50,832
気のせいだったらいやだから...
It'd suck if I just missed it...

316
00:21:50,932 --> 00:21:53,232
ちょ、ちょっと目開けていいよ。今いいよ。今目開けていいよ。
Wait, you can open your eyes a bit. It's fine now, you can open them.

317
00:21:53,332 --> 00:21:54,632
ないな...
It's not there...

318
00:21:54,732 --> 00:21:56,232
ないな...
It really isn't...

319
00:21:57,132 --> 00:21:58,532
ないよね...
There's none, right...?

320
00:22:00,332 --> 00:22:01,332
はい。
Okay.

321
00:22:01,832 --> 00:22:02,832
そうし...
In that ca—

322
00:22:03,532 --> 00:22:07,232
カタカナだよ、カタカナ。カタカナだよ、カタカナ。
In Katakana, yeah. I searched in Katakana.

323
00:22:09,132 --> 00:22:10,932
うん。なかった。
Yeah, it wasn't there.

324
00:22:11,132 --> 00:22:14,232
ガチでごめん！ガチでごめん、ガチでごめん！
Seriously, I'm so sorry! Seriously sorry, my bad!

325
00:22:14,532 --> 00:22:16,832
ど、どごめん！どごめん！
S-Super sorry! Super sorry!

326
00:22:17,732 --> 00:22:20,132
えーっと... どうしようかな。
Uhh... What should I do?

327
00:22:20,332 --> 00:22:22,232
目瞑っててね！
Keep your eyes closed!

328
00:22:22,332 --> 00:22:25,532
今、お主ら、いい？目瞑りよ。目瞑りよ。
Alright, everyone, got it? Close your eyes. Close your eyes.

329
00:22:25,832 --> 00:22:27,732
目瞑りよ！
Keep them closed!

330
00:22:27,932 --> 00:22:30,932
行くよ？行くよ！
Ready? Here goes!

331
00:22:31,232 --> 00:22:32,432
えー...
Uhh...

332
00:22:32,632 --> 00:22:36,832
はい、さ、さ、さ、ちょ、これで、こ、隠して、こう隠して、よしよしよし...
Okay, and, and, let me cover it like this, cover it this way, okay, okay, okay...

333
00:22:37,032 --> 00:22:38,932
ん？違う... あ、やばい。
Huh? Wait... Ah, shoot!

334
00:22:39,132 --> 00:22:42,032
こうして、こう、こう、こう、こう、よしよしよしよし！
Do this, and like this, this, this, okay okay okay!

335
00:22:42,132 --> 00:22:43,932
目開けていいよ！
You can open your eyes now!

336
00:22:44,332 --> 00:22:46,832
目開けていいよ、お主ら！
You can open your eyes, everyone!

337
00:22:47,032 --> 00:22:48,432
目開けていいよ。
You can open them.

338
00:22:48,832 --> 00:22:50,032
よいしょ。よしよしよしよし。
Whew, alright alright alright.

339
00:22:50,132 --> 00:22:53,732
はいはいはいはい、行けた！行けた行けた！行けた行けた。ちょちょちょちょ
Yes, yes, yes, I did it! I did it, I did it! Wait wait wait...

340
00:22:53,932 --> 00:22:56,332
ふー、危なかったー！
Phew, that was close!

341
00:22:56,532 --> 00:23:03,532
え、どうしよう。本当は、あの、30曲の中に入れてたステラを歌おうとしたんじゃけど、
Uh, what now? Truth is, I was going to sing Stella, which was on my 30-song list, but...

342
00:23:03,832 --> 00:23:07,732
ちょっとオケがなか... ちょ、これは本当にわしの準備不足だ。
There was no backing track... Ah, this was really poor preparation on my part.

343
00:23:08,532 --> 00:23:12,732
わしの準備不足で、あの、なかったので、
Due to my lack of preparation, it wasn't there, so...

344
00:23:13,032 --> 00:23:15,432
ちょ、一曲プロセカの曲歌うか。
Should I sing another Project Sekai song instead?

345
00:23:15,632 --> 00:23:18,032
違うプロセカの曲歌うか。
Let's sing a different Project Sekai song!

346
00:23:18,932 --> 00:23:21,832
一曲違うプロセカの曲歌うのじゃ。
I'll sing a different Project Sekai song!

347
00:23:22,632 --> 00:23:29,832
そう、なんか「これ歌おうかな」と思ったんだけど、ステラ歌... ステラの方歌おうかなと思ってやめたやつがあって、
Right, there was one where I thought, "Maybe I'll sing this," but held back because I wanted to sing Stella instead...

348
00:23:30,232 --> 00:23:33,832
や、やめたやつ... そう、そっち余ったから、うん。
The one I held back on... Yeah, that one's left over, so yep!

349
00:23:35,632 --> 00:23:36,932
うん、歌うのじゃ。
Yeah, I'll sing that one!

350
00:23:37,832 --> 00:23:42,232
えっと、ちょっとセトリに書けないから、
Um, since I can't write it on the setlist right now...

351
00:23:42,532 --> 00:23:44,232
えー...
Uhh...

352
00:23:44,332 --> 00:23:47,332
もう、ごめんね、わちゃわちゃしちゃって。
Geez, sorry for making such a fuss!

353
00:23:47,432 --> 00:23:51,632
本当にごめんね、お主ら。まったく。まったくね、困っちゃうのじゃ。
Truly sorry, everyone. Really... what a mess I've gotten myself into!

354
00:23:51,732 --> 00:23:52,932
えっと、
Um...

355
00:23:55,232 --> 00:23:56,832
あ、カタカナ。
Ah, Katakana.

356
00:23:57,032 --> 00:23:59,032
えー...
Uhh...

357
00:24:02,032 --> 00:24:06,032
よいしょ。よいしょ。はいはいはいはいはいはいはいはい。
Alright. There we go. Okay, okay, okay, okay...

358
00:24:06,332 --> 00:24:10,532
ちょ、1枚だけちょっと文字色が違うんだけど我慢してね。
Wait, the font color is slightly different for just this one, but bear with me!

359
00:24:10,732 --> 00:24:13,932
1枚だけ、1枚だけ、1枚だけね、あの、違うんだけどね。
Just this one, just one song's color is different, but...

360
00:24:14,032 --> 00:24:17,332
ま、気になる方は... A型の皆さんは気になるかな？
Well, for those who care... Maybe type A folks will be bothered by it?

361
00:24:17,432 --> 00:24:20,032
A型の皆さんは気になるかもしれないんだけど、
Type A folks might notice it, but...

362
00:24:21,332 --> 00:24:22,332
はい！
Alright!

363
00:24:22,532 --> 00:24:27,532
ちょっとじゃあ、あの、プロセカの書き下ろし曲、1曲歌おうかなと思って、
So I'll sing an original commission song from Project Sekai!

364
00:24:28,032 --> 00:24:30,832
歌うのじゃ！
Here I go!

365
00:24:32,532 --> 00:24:33,832
えっと...
Um...

366
00:24:33,932 --> 00:24:36,632
「サイバーパンクデッドボーイ」！
"Cyberpunk Dead Boy"!

367
00:24:37,532 --> 00:24:38,632
うん。
Yeah.

368
00:24:38,832 --> 00:24:46,032
なんかね、ステラとね、サイバーパンクデッドボーイをね、書いた記憶あり、あの30曲のやつに。
I remember writing down both Stella and Cyberpunk Dead Boy on that 30-song list.

369
00:24:46,232 --> 00:24:49,032
すごい好きなのじゃ、めっちゃかっこいい。めっちゃ...
I really love it, it's super cool. Super...

370
00:24:49,032 --> 00:24:52,232
あ！左下がサイバーパンクデッドボーイになっとる！
Ah! The bottom-left says Cyberpunk Dead Boy!

371
00:24:52,332 --> 00:24:54,432
助けてお主ら！どうしよう！
Help me, everyone! What do I do?!

372
00:24:54,532 --> 00:24:56,232
元々なんて書いたっけ？
What did it say originally?!

373
00:24:56,332 --> 00:24:59,832
え、ちょちょちょ待って。歌、歌、歌、歌、歌、歌部分の...
Wait, wait, wait, hold on. Song, song, song... "The singing portion..."

374
00:25:00,120 --> 00:25:02,200
ん？歌唱部...
Huh? "Singing part..."

375
00:25:02,200 --> 00:25:04,000
助けてー！
Help meee!

376
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:08,000
「歌唱部分の切り抜きは禁止なのじゃ」とか...
Like "Clipping the singing parts is prohibited"...

377
00:25:08,040 --> 00:25:10,240
あー！
Aaargh!

378
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:12,340
のじゃ... 待って。
...noja. Wait.

379
00:25:12,840 --> 00:25:14,340
こう... んー...
Like this... Hmmm...

380
00:25:16,040 --> 00:25:17,340
こうか！
Like this!

381
00:25:19,440 --> 00:25:22,340
助けて！面白い！わし歌歌いたいのに！
Help! This is hilarious! I just want to sing, though!

382
00:25:22,340 --> 00:25:25,540
わし、わし歌歌いたくてここに来たのに...
I... I came here because I wanted to sing...

383
00:25:25,540 --> 00:25:27,440
「よく気づいたね」
"Good catch."

384
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:28,440
はいはいはい。
Right, right, right.

385
00:25:28,440 --> 00:25:31,440
あ、行けた！いいんじゃない？え、わし、わし、わしキタ！
Oh, got it! Isn't this good? Wait, I... I'm on a roll!

386
00:25:31,440 --> 00:25:32,440
わし行けるわ。
I've got this.

387
00:25:32,440 --> 00:25:33,440
ごめん主等。
Sorry, everyone.

388
00:25:33,440 --> 00:25:35,040
わしすごいかも。
I might actually be amazing.

389
00:25:35,040 --> 00:25:36,540
わしできたかも。
I might have nailed it.

390
00:25:36,540 --> 00:25:38,940
全部理解した。ほら！文字の色とかも、ほら。
I figured it all out. Look! Even the font colors, look.

391
00:25:38,940 --> 00:25:40,440
合わせられちゃうかも。
I can even match them.

392
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:42,240
はい、神！
Boom, godlike!

393
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:44,240
よしよしよしよし。ふー、危なかった！
Alright, alright. Phew, that was close!

394
00:25:44,240 --> 00:25:45,740
何もなかったな？
Nothing happened, right?

395
00:25:45,740 --> 00:25:49,040
何もなかった。最初から、本日は『サイバーパンクデッドボーイ』を...
Nothing happened at all. From the start, today I was going to...

396
00:25:49,040 --> 00:25:50,540
歌うつもりだった。
...sing "Cyberpunk Dead Boy."

397
00:25:50,540 --> 00:25:51,640
本当か？
Really?

398
00:25:51,640 --> 00:25:53,040
行くのじゃ！
Let's do this!

399
00:25:53,040 --> 00:25:55,240
ちょ、飲酒してない！飲酒してない！
Hey, I haven't been drinking! I'm not drunk!

400
00:25:55,240 --> 00:25:57,640
飲酒してないって！抜けたって、酒！
I'm really not drunk! The alcohol's completely worn off!

401
00:25:57,640 --> 00:25:59,040
大丈夫なのじゃ。
Everything's fine-noja.

402
00:25:59,040 --> 00:26:01,340
やばい！まだ、まだ1曲しか歌ってない！
Oh no! I've still... I've still only sung one song!

403
00:26:01,340 --> 00:26:04,240
いつもなら、いつもならもう3、4曲は歌ってる時間なのに！
Normally, I'd have sung three or four songs by this time!

404
00:26:04,240 --> 00:26:05,840
まずい！
This is bad!

405
00:26:06,040 --> 00:26:09,540
よーし、よしよしよし、大丈夫。大丈夫大丈夫。
Alright, there we go, I'm okay. I'm totally fine.

406
00:26:09,540 --> 00:26:13,840
よしよしよし。そして、BGMを切って、エコーをかけて...
Alright. And now, I turn off the BGM, turn on the echo...

407
00:26:13,840 --> 00:26:15,540
はいはいはいはい。
Okay, okay, okay.

408
00:26:15,540 --> 00:26:17,340
酔ってないって！
I said I'm not drunk!

409
00:26:18,840 --> 00:26:21,040
酔ってないって。え？
I'm not drunk. Huh?

410
00:26:21,040 --> 00:26:24,040
でも元々『サイバーパンクデッドボーイ』を歌うつもりがなかったから...
But since I didn't originally plan to sing "Cyberpunk Dead Boy"...

411
00:26:24,040 --> 00:26:26,540
上手に歌える自信は... ちょ、言い訳ダサい！
...my confidence in singing it well is... Wait, making excuses is lame!

412
00:26:26,540 --> 00:26:27,840
言い訳ダサいのじゃ！
Making excuses is so uncool-noja!

413
00:26:27,840 --> 00:26:29,540
行くのじゃー！
Let's just do it!

414
00:26:30,040 --> 00:26:32,440
言い訳ダサいのじゃ！
Making excuses is so lame-noja!

415
00:26:33,840 --> 00:26:35,840
やばいぜ。行くのじゃん！
Oh man. Here we go!

416
00:26:46,240 --> 00:26:50,240
お書きになったそんな音楽は現在使われておりません もう一度お書き直しください
"The music you have composed is not currently in use. Please rewrite it once more."

417
00:26:50,740 --> 00:26:53,040
意味わかんねぇ！
What the hell does that even mean?!

418
00:26:56,840 --> 00:26:59,040
意味わかんねぇ！
Makes no damn sense!

419
00:27:04,240 --> 00:27:07,440
どーせ誰も聴いてなんかないさ
Nobody's listening anyway, right?

420
00:27:07,440 --> 00:27:11,040
音楽なんて全部ファッション 音亡 喰らって選手退場 ワンナイト
Music is all just fashion, swallowed by sound and ejected in one night.

421
00:27:11,040 --> 00:27:14,040
どーせ何も伝えてなんかないさ
Not conveying a single thing anyway, right?

422
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:17,340
なんとかトック撮って売名 あんな気取っておいて最低 グンナイ
Filming some TikTok to get famous, posing like that is just the lowest. Good night.

423
00:27:17,340 --> 00:27:21,040
どうしたってどうみたって 尊師たちでもう大渋滞
No matter what or how you look at it, it's jammed full of self-styled gurus already.

424
00:27:21,040 --> 00:27:24,740
それでも あっち、こっち、そっち、ぼっち、 卍 Zエイジ 猿も欲しがる
Still, over here, over there, all alone, Gen Z and even monkeys want it.

425
00:27:24,740 --> 00:27:28,040
パンチライン欲しいの 意味とかどっちだっていいよ
I want a punchline, who cares about the meaning either way?

426
00:27:28,040 --> 00:27:32,040
歌詞とかどうでもいいので ノれるのください
Nobody cares about the lyrics, so just give me a beat I can vibe to.

427
00:27:32,040 --> 00:27:35,040
さぁ皆で笑いましょう
Come on, let's all laugh together!

428
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:38,340
芸術より数の大小？ ヴァイラスに酷い代償
Numbers over art, is that it? A terrible price to pay for going viral.

429
00:27:38,340 --> 00:27:41,840
じゃあどうすんの？それでいいんだっけ？
So whatcha gonna do? Was that really fine?

430
00:27:41,840 --> 00:27:44,840
頭は空回り死んでいく
My head spins in circles, rotting away.

431
00:27:46,240 --> 00:27:49,540
ふざけるな バイバイ バズメロディー
Don't mess with me, bye-bye viral melody.

432
00:27:49,540 --> 00:27:52,740
疑えよ大概嘘ばかり
Doubt it, it's mostly full of lies anyway.

433
00:27:52,740 --> 00:27:56,040
化けんな 幻想でも理想でも良い
Don't disguise yourself, whether an illusion or an ideal, it's fine.

434
00:27:56,040 --> 00:27:59,340
君の歌いたかった物はどうしたんだい？
What happened to what you really wanted to sing?

435
00:27:59,340 --> 00:28:02,540
ぶざまでも オーライ 嘘じゃない
Even if it's unsightly, that's alright, it's no lie.

436
00:28:02,540 --> 00:28:05,740
お金や擬奏で満たす前に
Before you fill yourself up with money and pretenses...

437
00:28:05,740 --> 00:28:08,840
負けんな 覚醒せよ鼓動達よ
Don't give up! Wake up, heartbeats!

438
00:28:08,840 --> 00:28:10,840
君の伝えたかった物はどうしたんだい？
What happened to the message you wanted to convey?

439
00:28:10,840 --> 00:28:12,640
意味わかんねぇ
Makes no damn sense!

440
00:28:13,240 --> 00:28:14,840
助かった、助かった...
Made it through, made it through...

441
00:28:15,040 --> 00:28:17,340
ガチここの、この曲の一番いいとこここ！
Seriously, this part... this is the best part of the song!

442
00:28:17,340 --> 00:28:19,440
「てーてっ、てーてー」のところ！
The "te-te, te-te" part!

443
00:28:19,440 --> 00:28:21,840
ガチかっこいい！ガチでかっこいい！
It's seriously so cool! Seriously cool!

444
00:28:21,840 --> 00:28:23,240
ガチでありがとう！
Seriously, thank you!

445
00:28:24,040 --> 00:28:27,340
お書きになったそんな音楽は現在使われておりません
"The music you have composed is not currently in use."

446
00:28:27,340 --> 00:28:30,840
ポップソング、ヒットソング聴いて もう一度お書き直してください
"Please listen to pop songs and hit songs, and rewrite it once more."

447
00:28:30,840 --> 00:28:33,540
あーもう ハイカラ作家ばっか 洒落臭いわ
Ah, seriously, those smug highbrow writers are so obnoxious!

448
00:28:33,540 --> 00:28:36,740
どいつも こいつも そいつも あいつも
This one, that one, him, her, all of them!

449
00:28:36,740 --> 00:28:38,840
意味わかんねぇ！
Makes no damn sense!

450
00:28:38,840 --> 00:28:42,540
どうしたってどうみたって 尊師たちでもう大渋滞
No matter what or how you look at it, it's jammed full of self-styled gurus already.

451
00:28:42,540 --> 00:28:46,040
それでも あっち、こっち、そっち、ぼっち、 卍 Zエイジ 猿も欲しがる
Still, over here, over there, all alone, Gen Z and even monkeys want it.

452
00:28:46,040 --> 00:28:49,540
パンチライン欲しいの 意味とかどっちだっていいよ
I want a punchline, who cares about the meaning either way?

453
00:28:49,540 --> 00:28:53,340
歌詞とかどうでもいいので 伸びるの下さい
Nobody cares about the lyrics, so just give me something that goes viral.

454
00:28:53,340 --> 00:28:56,540
さぁ皆で祓いましょう
Come on, let's all exorcise it together!

455
00:28:56,540 --> 00:28:59,840
芸術より数なんでしょう？ ヴァイラスに酷い代償
It's all about numbers over art, right? A terrible price to pay for going viral.

456
00:28:59,840 --> 00:29:03,040
じゃあどうすんの？ それでいいんだっけ？
So whatcha gonna do? Was that really fine?

457
00:29:03,040 --> 00:29:06,040
頭は空回り死んでいく
My head spins in circles, rotting away.

458
00:29:06,240 --> 00:29:09,540
ふざけるな バイバイ バズメロディー
Don't mess with me, bye-bye viral melody.

459
00:29:09,540 --> 00:29:12,740
疑えよ大概嘘ばかり
Doubt it, it's mostly full of lies anyway.

460
00:29:12,740 --> 00:29:16,040
化けんな 幻想でも理想でも良い
Don't disguise yourself, whether an illusion or an ideal, it's fine.

461
00:29:16,040 --> 00:29:19,340
君の歌いたかった物はどうしたんだい？
What happened to what you really wanted to sing?

462
00:29:19,340 --> 00:29:22,540
このままじゃ 到底 終われない
There's no way it can end like this.

463
00:29:22,540 --> 00:29:25,840
欲しいのは きっと お金じゃない
What I want definitely isn't money.

464
00:29:25,840 --> 00:29:28,940
負けんな 覚醒せよ 鼓動達よ
Don't give up! Wake up, heartbeats!

465
00:29:28,940 --> 00:29:32,040
君の歌いたかった物がきっとあるんだ
There's definitely a song that you wanted to sing!

466
00:29:32,040 --> 00:29:33,440
ふざけるな…
Don't mess with me...

467
00:29:33,440 --> 00:29:36,740
ふざけるな バイバイ バズメロディー
Don't mess with me, bye-bye viral melody.

468
00:29:36,740 --> 00:29:39,940
疑えよ大概嘘ばかり
Doubt it, it's mostly full of lies anyway.

469
00:29:39,940 --> 00:29:43,240
化けんな 幻想でも理想でも良い
Don't disguise yourself, whether an illusion or an ideal, it's fine.

470
00:29:43,240 --> 00:29:46,540
君の歌いたかった物はどうしたんだい？
What happened to what you really wanted to sing?

471
00:29:46,540 --> 00:29:49,840
ぶざまでも オーライ 嘘じゃない
Even if it's unsightly, that's alright, it's no lie.

472
00:29:49,840 --> 00:29:53,040
お金や擬奏で満たす前に
Before you fill yourself up with money and pretenses...

473
00:29:53,040 --> 00:29:56,040
負けんな 覚醒せよ 鼓動達よ
Don't give up! Wake up, heartbeats!

474
00:29:56,040 --> 00:29:57,340
僕の伝えたかった物はどうしたんだい？
What happened to the message I wanted to convey?

475
00:29:57,340 --> 00:29:58,740
意味わかんねぇ！！！！！！！！
What the hell does that even mean?!

476
00:29:58,740 --> 00:30:00,088
意味わかんねぇよ！！！！！！！
Makes no damn sense!

477
00:30:01,908 --> 00:30:05,198
たん たか たん たか たか たん たか たか たん
Tan taka tan taka taka tan taka taka tan...

478
00:30:13,888 --> 00:30:16,898
たん たか たん たん たん
Tan taka tan tan tan...

479
00:30:16,898 --> 00:30:19,498
たん たか たん たん たん
Tan taka tan tan tan...

480
00:30:21,448 --> 00:30:24,128
意味わかんねぇー！
Makes no damn sense!

481
00:30:26,548 --> 00:30:28,228
いぇーい。
Yeah!

482
00:30:31,098 --> 00:30:36,608
サイバーパンクデッドボーイでしたのじゃー！わしこの曲かっこよくて大好き！
That was "Cyberpunk Dead Boy"! I love this song, it's so cool!

483
00:30:37,798 --> 00:30:40,398
めちゃくちゃかっこいい曲ー！
Such an insanely cool song!

484
00:30:40,498 --> 00:30:44,248
やっぱね、あのね、わしね、わしがね、
You know, for me...

485
00:30:44,248 --> 00:30:47,348
好きな曲はいっぱいあるんじゃけど、特に！特に！
There are tons of songs I love, but especially, especially!

486
00:30:47,348 --> 00:30:52,348
あの、かっこいい曲を可愛い声の女の子が歌うキャラソンが大好きで。
I just love character songs where a girl with a super cute voice sings a really cool track.

487
00:30:52,728 --> 00:30:56,168
で、まあ、あの、ワンダショの曲？
And well, this Wonder Show song...

488
00:30:56,168 --> 00:31:00,648
ワンダショ書き下ろし曲じゃから、もちろん男性ももちろん歌唱してるんじゃけど、
Since it was written for Wonder Show, the guys sing in it too, of course, but...

489
00:31:00,798 --> 00:31:04,468
あのね、プロセカのね、えむちゃんってキャラの声がすっごいきゅるっきゅるで可愛くて！
Emu-chan from Proseka has such an adorable, squeaky-clean voice!

490
00:31:04,598 --> 00:31:08,798
きゅるっきゅるで可愛い子がね、このちょっ治安悪めのね、治安悪めの、
Having such a sparkly-cute girl sing this kind of rough-and-tumble...

491
00:31:08,928 --> 00:31:13,448
あの、ジャカジャカしたね、ジャカジャカしたかっこいい曲をね、
gritty, fast and driving, cool track...

492
00:31:13,448 --> 00:31:17,368
可愛く歌うのがめっちゃ好き！めっちゃ好き！
singing it so cutely—I love that so much! I love it!

493
00:31:18,048 --> 00:31:21,098
めちゃくちゃ好きですのじゃ。自分で可愛い言った？
I really love it. Wait, did I call myself cute?

494
00:31:21,248 --> 00:31:23,748
ん？わしも可愛いよ？
Huh? I'm cute too, though!

495
00:31:23,748 --> 00:31:27,548
「わしら可愛い？」「わしら、わしも可愛い？」ふふふ
"Are we cute?" "We are... Am I cute too?" Hehehe.

496
00:31:27,648 --> 00:31:33,298
え、そう、だ、同様の理由で、あの、以前ミスコンダクターが好きって話をしたことがあると思うんじゃけど、
Right! For the exact same reason—I think I mentioned before that I love "Misconductor"—

497
00:31:33,398 --> 00:31:37,498
かっこいい曲をね、可愛いボーカルの女の子が歌うのが大好きじゃから、
because I adore when cool songs are sung by girls with cute vocals,

498
00:31:37,628 --> 00:31:42,268
だからミスコンダクターって曲の、あの、複数人が歌唱してるバージョンがあるんじゃけど、
in "Misconductor", there are versions sung by multiple people,

499
00:31:42,268 --> 00:31:48,348
中でもキィって子が歌唱してるのが好きな理由は、可愛い女の子が歌ってるのが好きだからなのじゃ。うん。
but the reason I like the version sung by Kii best is simply because I love hearing a cute girl sing it. Yep.

500
00:31:48,848 --> 00:31:54,448
ちょっと早口になっちゃった。くふふふ。ちょ、ちょっと早口になっちゃったか？ちょっと早口になっちゃったか。
I started talking way too fast. Hehehe. Did I talk a bit too fast? Maybe just a little.

501
00:31:54,448 --> 00:31:57,698
まあそういうこともね、あるよねー。そういうこともあるよね。
Well, that kind of thing happens, right? It sure does.

502
00:31:57,698 --> 00:32:04,248
そう、あの、この曲は原曲者さんもね、歌ってたり、歌ってる版があったり、あの、ボカロ版もあったりして、
Right, for this song, the original creator sang a version too, and there's a Vocaloid version...

503
00:32:04,248 --> 00:32:06,498
色んなのがあるんじゃけど。
There are all sorts of versions,

504
00:32:06,498 --> 00:32:10,748
そう、中でもね、やっぱ、あの、書き下ろし版も結構ね、わしね、好きなんだよね。
but I really love the commissioned game version too.

505
00:32:13,298 --> 00:32:16,898
のじゃ。早口トークしちゃった。
Yep. Went on a total fast-talking tangent.

506
00:32:17,998 --> 00:32:20,498
早口オタク君出ちゃった。
My fast-talking otaku mode totally slipped out.

507
00:32:20,498 --> 00:32:22,498
それでは！
Alright then!

508
00:32:22,498 --> 00:32:25,848
えっーと、ん？ん？
Let's see... Huh? Wait.

509
00:32:27,548 --> 00:32:30,848
ちょっと待ってね。どうなってんだ？
Hold on a second. What's going on here?

510
00:32:31,798 --> 00:32:33,848
ん？ほうか。
Huh? Oh, I see.

511
00:32:37,048 --> 00:32:38,298
白。
White.

512
00:32:38,998 --> 00:32:41,548
白。あ、なるほど、こうなってんのね。了解。
White. Ah, I see, that's how it is. Got it.

513
00:32:41,548 --> 00:32:44,248
よし！よしよしよしよし。
Alright! Alright, alright, alright.

514
00:32:44,248 --> 00:32:48,598
ちょ、PNGをね、一、ちょっとだけ表示させた。PNGをちょっとだけ表示させた。
I briefly displayed the PNG. Just showed the PNG for a second.

515
00:32:48,598 --> 00:32:51,948
これでいいか。これでいいか、いけるか？辻褄が合うか。
Is this good? Will this work? Does it line up?

516
00:32:51,948 --> 00:32:54,898
もうちょい上か？こんなもんか。
A little higher? How about this?

517
00:32:55,248 --> 00:33:02,198
ということで、次の曲歌っていこうと思うのじゃー！えーっと、えーっと、
And with that, I'm going to sing the next song! Let's see, let's see...

518
00:33:04,298 --> 00:33:10,098
そう、なんとね！わし、わしの大好きなね、Across the line がね、
Guess what?! My absolute favorite song, "Across the line"...

519
00:33:10,098 --> 00:33:17,198
JOYSOUND... カラオケ配信者 JOYSOUND に入ってたの！入ってたの！
It was in JOYSOUND! The Karaoke Streamer JOYSOUND catalog had it! It was actually there!

520
00:33:17,298 --> 00:33:24,798
そう、わしの大好きな、わしの大好きな曲がね、なんと入ってたので歌っちゃおうと思うのじゃ。
Yes, my favorite, absolute favorite song was there, so I just had to sing it!

521
00:33:25,048 --> 00:33:33,498
あの、『中二病でも恋がしたい！』の、映画か、あれ？映画の曲か？
It's from "Love, Chunibyo & Other Delusions"... Was it the movie? A movie track?

522
00:33:36,048 --> 00:33:42,998
キャラソン？あれ何だ、挿入歌か？キャラソンじゃけど、あれ何て言う枠なんだろう。
A character song? Wait, is it an insert song? It's a character song, but what category would that fall under?

523
00:33:42,998 --> 00:33:46,898
の曲でございますのじゃ！
...Anyway, it's that song!

524
00:33:46,898 --> 00:33:52,498
よし、歌っちゃう。歌っちゃうのじゃー！
Alright, I'm gonna sing it. Here I go!

525
00:33:52,498 --> 00:33:56,848
そう、ZAQさん、作詞どころかもう作曲もやってらっしゃるよ。
Yeah, ZAQ-san didn't just write the lyrics, she composed it too!

526
00:33:56,848 --> 00:34:06,048
てか、『中二病でも恋がしたい！』の曲は、あの、キャラソンとかも含めてかなり彼女がやっている... え、全部やってるよね？
Actually, for "Love, Chunibyo & Other Delusions", she did pretty much all the songs, including character songs... Wait, did she do all of them?

527
00:34:06,048 --> 00:34:11,898
なんか劇伴以外やってる気がするけど、どうじゃろ？うん。
I feel like she did everything except the background score, right? Yeah.

528
00:34:12,248 --> 00:34:17,198
映画の劇中歌かな？歌いますのじゃー！
An insert song from the movie, I think? Time to sing it!

529
00:34:18,048 --> 00:34:22,298
よいしょ。BGM消して、エコーをつけて、よし。
Alright. Turn off the BGM, add some echo, and ready.

530
00:34:23,048 --> 00:34:25,048
いくのじゃー！
Here we go~!

531
00:34:50,198 --> 00:34:55,348
眠る前に抱きしめた
The pillow I held close before going to sleep...

532
00:34:55,348 --> 00:35:00,048
あの枕に君を重ねた後
After seeing you in it...

533
00:35:02,316 --> 00:35:07,506
水平線の 向こう側にいる
On the other side of the horizon...

534
00:35:07,756 --> 00:35:11,506
君の夢をみた
...I had a dream of you.

535
00:35:14,356 --> 00:35:19,456
根拠のない強さも 理由だらけの弱さも
Both groundless strength and weakness full of reasons...

536
00:35:19,856 --> 00:35:25,256
お互い抱きしめ合えたから
...because we could embrace them in each other...

537
00:35:25,656 --> 00:35:32,456
あの頃の痛みは 風に乱れ散ったよ
...the pain from back then scattered in the wind.

538
00:35:34,356 --> 00:35:37,456
向こう側に連れていって
Take me over to the other side.

539
00:35:37,556 --> 00:35:43,956
恋しいから泣いた だけど愛しいからもっと笑った
I cried because I missed you, but smiled even more because I adore you.

540
00:35:44,256 --> 00:35:49,056
「いなくなる」と怯えるより 信じるほうが尊いなぁ
Rather than fearing you'll disappear, believing is so much more precious.

541
00:35:49,356 --> 00:35:55,856
今がどんどん重なって 君の日々を彩っていく
These present moments pile up, bringing color to your days.

542
00:35:56,256 --> 00:36:00,856
私の存在は 何色をしてる?
What color is my existence?

543
00:36:01,056 --> 00:36:08,556
これは解けない魔法 「たぶんずっと すきだよ」を誓うね
This is unbreakable magic. I vow that I'll probably love you forever.

544
00:36:19,556 --> 00:36:25,656
ノスタルジックな心の核は
The nostalgic core of my heart...

545
00:36:25,956 --> 00:36:29,856
いらない羽根で固まる
...is hardened with needless feathers.

546
00:36:31,756 --> 00:36:37,356
いくら探してみても 想いぶつけてみても
No matter how much I searched, no matter how much I poured out my feelings...

547
00:36:37,456 --> 00:36:42,056
白さは屈折すると思ってた
...I thought that pure whiteness would just refract.

548
00:36:42,456 --> 00:36:49,556
予期しない場所からふいに抱きしめられて
Suddenly embraced from an unexpected place...

549
00:36:51,656 --> 00:36:55,056
共鳴しあう出会い
...an encounter that resonates together.

550
00:36:55,256 --> 00:37:00,856
思い出したくない景色ほど 色あせずに残る
Sceneries I don't want to recall remain unfaded...

551
00:37:01,156 --> 00:37:06,856
恥ずかしくて会えないのに 君の名を呼んじゃうなぁ
...and though I'm too embarrassed to see you, I still call your name.

552
00:37:07,156 --> 00:37:13,656
無慈悲な直感が導きだす二人の運命
A merciless intuition guides our two destinies.

553
00:37:13,956 --> 00:37:18,456
弾ける効果線 閃くような未来
Popping action lines, a flashing future.

554
00:37:18,756 --> 00:37:25,756
君の手を握ったよ なんだか笑顔まで似てきたね
I took your hand; somehow even our smiles have grown alike.

555
00:37:48,556 --> 00:37:51,756
向こう側に連れていって
Take me over to the other side.

556
00:37:51,856 --> 00:37:57,656
小さな部屋の扉 あけて 大きな世界が泳いでる
Open the door to this tiny room, a vast world is swimming out there.

557
00:37:57,956 --> 00:38:03,856
煌めく目を細める君 そっちの方に今行くね
You squint your sparkling eyes, I'm heading over to you.

558
00:38:04,056 --> 00:38:10,256
恋しいから泣いた だけど愛しいからもっと笑った
I cried because I missed you, but smiled even more because I adore you.

559
00:38:10,456 --> 00:38:15,356
「いなくなる」と怯えるより 信じるほうが尊いなぁ
Rather than fearing you'll disappear, believing is so much more precious.

560
00:38:15,656 --> 00:38:22,056
今がどんどん重なって 君の日々を彩っていく
These present moments pile up, bringing color to your days.

561
00:38:22,356 --> 00:38:26,956
私の存在は 何色をしてる?
What color is my existence?

562
00:38:27,156 --> 00:38:35,056
これは解けない魔法 「たぶんずっと すきだよ」を誓うね
This is unbreakable magic. I vow that I'll probably love you forever.

563
00:38:48,856 --> 00:38:54,656
のじゃ〜！Across the lineでしたのじゃ〜！
Noja~! That was 'Across the line', noja~!

564
00:38:56,456 --> 00:38:58,756
あのね、コメント欄でバレてた。
You know, people in the chat totally noticed.

565
00:38:58,956 --> 00:39:02,056
あの声優さんがね、内田真礼さんなんじゃけど、
The voice actress is Maaya Uchida-san, but...

566
00:39:02,156 --> 00:39:04,656
ちょ寄せてたのバレてた。
...they caught on that I was trying to imitate her voice!

567
00:39:05,156 --> 00:39:07,156
寄せて、寄せて歌ってみたのじゃ。
I tried leaning into her style while singing, noja.

568
00:39:07,356 --> 00:39:10,256
なんでかって、原曲が大好き！
Why? Because I love the original song so much!

569
00:39:11,156 --> 00:39:13,656
Across the lineが大好き！
I just love 'Across the line'!

570
00:39:13,856 --> 00:39:18,956
そう、そうそう、僕ね、実はね歌っていてね、それがねバレていた。
Yeah, exactly! I was actually singing like that, and people totally noticed.

571
00:39:19,456 --> 00:39:22,256
バレてましたのじゃ。
I got caught red-handed, noja!

572
00:39:22,556 --> 00:39:26,156
そうなんだよ、わしさ、あの内田真礼さん好きでさ、
That's right! I really love Maaya Uchida-san...

573
00:39:26,356 --> 00:39:28,956
この曲知ったのもね、あの、
...and the way I learned about this song...

574
00:39:29,856 --> 00:39:34,256
あの、わしの曲を知る経緯って多分結構変。
...well, the backstory of how I discover music is probably pretty weird.

575
00:39:34,456 --> 00:39:36,556
変なんだけど、えー、
It's weird, but, um...

576
00:39:36,656 --> 00:39:45,356
まず内田真礼さんのアーティスト、その声優さんとしてではなく声優アーティストとしての楽曲が好きだった。
First of all, I loved Maaya Uchida-san's songs as an artist—not just as a voice actress, but as a voice actress music artist.

577
00:39:46,056 --> 00:39:49,856
そう、なんかスマイリングスパイラルの話とかしたことあると思うんじゃけど、
Yeah, I think I've mentioned 'Smiling Spiral' before...

578
00:39:50,056 --> 00:39:54,056
そう、内田真礼さんのアーティストとしての曲を聴いていた。
...so yeah, I was listening to Maaya Uchida-san's music released as a solo artist.

579
00:39:54,356 --> 00:39:56,256
んで、あの、
And then, um...

580
00:39:56,456 --> 00:39:59,856
そこね、内田真礼さんが声優として歌唱してるキャラソン...
...from there, the character songs that Maaya Uchida-san sang in character...

581
00:40:00,064 --> 00:40:02,224
を、全部聴いていた中で、
...while listening through all of them,

582
00:40:03,004 --> 00:40:06,164
えっと、「Across the line」を見つける。
um, I found "Across the line".

583
00:40:06,764 --> 00:40:09,184
「めっちゃええやん！なんじゃこの曲！？」と思う。
I was like, "This is amazing! What even is this song?!"

584
00:40:10,284 --> 00:40:16,884
んで、わしがあの、すごい好きな作家の中にね、ZAQさんがいて、ZAQさんっていう作家さんがすごい好きなんじゃけど、
And you know, among the songwriters I really love is ZAQ-san. I really love this composer named ZAQ-san...

585
00:40:17,124 --> 00:40:19,064
あの、そこでZAQさんを知るの。
That was actually how I discovered ZAQ-san.

586
00:40:19,524 --> 00:40:20,144
そう。
Yeah.

587
00:40:20,364 --> 00:40:25,924
内田真礼さんが歌ってるからで聴いたら、「なんじゃこの曲！？めっちゃええ！」と思って、
I listened to it because Maaya Uchida-san was singing it, and when I did, I thought, "What is this song?! It's so good!"

588
00:40:26,604 --> 00:40:27,524
あのー、
And...

589
00:40:28,224 --> 00:40:28,824
そう。
Yeah.

590
00:40:29,104 --> 00:40:31,764
「なんじゃこの作詞作曲！？」と思って、
I thought, "Who wrote and composed this?!"

591
00:40:31,964 --> 00:40:37,004
初めて歌を聴いてるときに、歌ってる人じゃなくて作ってる人に
And for the first time while listening to music, instead of the person singing,

592
00:40:37,144 --> 00:40:39,984
目を向け始めたのがここ。
I started paying attention to the creator. That was right here.

593
00:40:40,284 --> 00:40:46,524
そう。それまでは、誰が作ってるかより誰が歌ってるかで曲を聴くことのほうが多かったんじゃけど、
Yeah. Up until then, I mostly listened to songs based on who was singing rather than who wrote them,

594
00:40:46,784 --> 00:40:47,404
そう。
yeah.

595
00:40:47,564 --> 00:40:51,104
ここで初めて作家さんの存在を意識して、
That was the first time I became conscious of composers,

596
00:40:51,264 --> 00:40:55,044
そう、意識して、「え、ZAQさんってやべえ！」と思って、こう、
and realizing that, I was like, "Whoa, ZAQ-san is incredible!" So...

597
00:40:55,284 --> 00:41:03,324
ZAQさんの曲をこう、何？あの、一覧で全部、とりあえずZAQさんが提供した曲は全部聴く、みたいなのをし始めて、
I looked up a list of all her songs and started listening to everything ZAQ-san had written.

598
00:41:03,504 --> 00:41:09,064
そう、じゃから、それこそみお先輩とかがさ、前のホロドリでさ、「Howling」がさ、
Yeah, that's why, when Mio-senpai and others performed "Howling" at the previous Holo Dori...

599
00:41:09,184 --> 00:41:14,344
あの、あったと思うんじゃけどさ、とかを知ったのも、その彼女が提供していたから、みたいな。
...the reason I knew about that song was because she was the one who wrote it.

600
00:41:14,764 --> 00:41:16,204
そう、感じ。
Yeah, exactly like that.

601
00:41:16,424 --> 00:41:21,064
そう、そっからね、作曲者さん、誰が作ったかをすごい意識するようになって、
From then on, I became super conscious of composers and who created each track,

602
00:41:21,284 --> 00:41:25,104
その、まあ彼女以外にも、他のそのアニソンの作家さんだったり、
and besides her, with other anime song composers as well...

603
00:41:25,324 --> 00:41:31,604
そう、が、「え、この人他にどういう曲書いてるんだろう？」みたいなのを、あの、聴くようになったのじゃ。
I started checking them out, wondering, "I wonder what other songs this person has written?"

604
00:41:32,184 --> 00:41:32,804
そう。
Yeah.

605
00:41:33,304 --> 00:41:40,884
そう、だからわしが結構曲を誰が作ったかを意識して聴き始めたきっかけの曲が「Across the line」で。
So, the song that sparked me to start paying attention to who wrote the music was "Across the line".

606
00:41:41,184 --> 00:41:44,844
そう、「Across the line」があまりにも曲として好きすぎて、
I just loved "Across the line" way too much as a song,

607
00:41:45,084 --> 00:41:47,344
曲として好きすぎて、
loved it way too much as a song...

608
00:41:47,704 --> 00:41:48,864
あのー、
Um...

609
00:41:49,084 --> 00:41:49,864
何？
What was it?

610
00:41:51,004 --> 00:41:52,264
そこから？
From there?

611
00:41:52,804 --> 00:41:56,084
そこから、なんか、わしの楽曲オタクが始まった。
From there, my life as a music nerd began.

612
00:41:56,584 --> 00:41:57,104
そう。
Yeah.

613
00:41:57,304 --> 00:42:00,664
そこからわしの楽曲オタクが始まった。
That was the start of my music nerd journey.

614
00:42:01,264 --> 00:42:01,884
ん？
Hm?

615
00:42:02,884 --> 00:42:04,464
ということなのじゃ。
That's how it happened.

616
00:42:05,204 --> 00:42:12,704
んで、だからわしはこの曲を先に聴いて、そっからあの『中二病でも恋がしたい！』を1期から見たっていう。
And so, I actually listened to this song first, and only then did I watch Love, Chunibyo & Other Delusions! from season 1.

617
00:42:12,984 --> 00:42:18,644
順番が変なの！曲から、そう、アニメを見始めるみたいな、
The order was totally backwards! Going from the song to watching the anime,

618
00:42:18,804 --> 00:42:20,964
ことがね、多い子供だった。うん。
I was a kid who often did things like that. Yup.

619
00:42:21,884 --> 00:42:22,484
そう。
Yeah.

620
00:42:23,804 --> 00:42:27,304
そう、始まりの曲なのじゃ。そう。
Yeah, it's the song where it all began for me. Truly.

621
00:42:27,524 --> 00:42:35,424
そう、だから映画の劇中歌から、「何だ！？」と思って、あの、1期を見るみたいな。
Yeah, discovering an insert song from a movie, going "What is this?!", and then watching season 1.

622
00:42:35,844 --> 00:42:39,184
そうそうそうそう、アニメを見に行くみたいな感じだったのじゃ。
Right, right, that's how I ended up checking out the anime.

623
00:42:39,604 --> 00:42:40,864
そうそうそうそうそう。
Right, right, exactly.

624
00:42:41,104 --> 00:42:43,744
え、そうそう！内田真礼さんからのZAQさん、わかるじゃろ？
Yeah, exactly! Discovering ZAQ-san through Maaya Uchida-san, you get it, right?

625
00:42:43,904 --> 00:42:49,244
そう、内田真礼さん、そのアーティスト曲とかも結構ZAQさんが何曲か提供しておられたり、
ZAQ-san has composed quite a few songs for Maaya Uchida-san's solo artist work,

626
00:42:49,504 --> 00:42:51,984
そう、なんか関係性が結構あるから。
so there's quite a strong connection between them.

627
00:42:52,044 --> 00:42:53,064
そうそうそうそうそう。
Right, right, exactly.

628
00:42:53,104 --> 00:42:55,264
そこからね、入ったのじゃ。うん。
That's how I got into it. Yup.

629
00:42:55,764 --> 00:42:57,204
そうそうそうそうそう。
Right, right, exactly.

630
00:42:57,504 --> 00:43:02,904
だから、割とね、どの曲でもね、わしはね、あれかもね。
So, no matter the song, my way...

631
00:43:03,104 --> 00:43:07,524
曲の知り方が変かも。変なことが多いかもしれない。うん。
...the way I discover music might be weird. It's often pretty weird. Yup.

632
00:43:08,584 --> 00:43:09,184
ね。
Right?

633
00:43:09,344 --> 00:43:14,704
でもそういう、いろんなね、入り口があるってすごい素敵なことだなああてわし思う。
But having so many different entry points like that is really wonderful, I think.

634
00:43:15,184 --> 00:43:19,484
それこそVTuberさんも。え、なんかね、VTuberさんのオリ曲も結構わし聴くんだよ。
The same goes for VTubers too. Like, I listen to a lot of original songs by VTubers.

635
00:43:19,524 --> 00:43:20,204
聴くの。
I really do.

636
00:43:20,704 --> 00:43:26,104
そう、だから、あのー、「この曲いいな」みたいな。
Yeah, so I'll be like, "Oh, this song is great."

637
00:43:26,304 --> 00:43:32,464
その、配信はあんまり見たことないけど、この人のこの曲いいな、みたいなのが結構何曲もね、
Even if I haven't watched their streams much, I often find songs where I think, "I really like this song from this person!"

638
00:43:32,704 --> 00:43:34,044
あったりね、するのじゃ。
There are quite a few like that.

639
00:43:35,104 --> 00:43:36,164
そうなのじゃ。
That's how it is.

640
00:43:36,584 --> 00:43:37,104
うん。
Yup.

641
00:43:39,004 --> 00:43:44,264
そして、えーと、ちょ、ちょっとね、ちょっと、ちょっとしたおしゃべりをしたところで、次何じゃったかな？
And now, um, after chatting a little bit, what was next again?

642
00:43:45,084 --> 00:43:48,024
あ、ボカロきた！おぬしらボカロきた！
Ah, Vocaloid is here! You guys, Vocaloid has arrived!

643
00:43:48,264 --> 00:43:50,064
ボカロ聴きたかったんじゃないのおぬしら！？
Weren't you guys wanting to hear some Vocaloid?!

644
00:43:50,904 --> 00:43:55,764
おぬしら、最近わしが、最近わしが、
Everyone, recently I... recently I...

645
00:43:57,064 --> 00:43:58,264
あのー、な、何だ？
Um, wh-what was it?

646
00:44:00,884 --> 00:44:06,664
ボカロ以外を歌いすぎ、あ、ボカロ？まあ『サイバーパンクデッドボーイ』ボカロっつったらボカロか。まあボカロか。
...sang too much non-Vocaloid... Wait, Vocaloid? Well, Cyberpunk Dead Boy is Vocaloid if you count it. Yeah, it's Vocaloid.

647
00:44:07,084 --> 00:44:08,564
失礼いたしました。
My apologies.

648
00:44:08,884 --> 00:44:09,984
失礼いたしました。
My apologies!

649
00:44:10,564 --> 00:44:14,764
ボカロ聴きたかったんじゃない？と思って、用意してきましたのじゃ！
I thought, "They probably want to hear Vocaloid, right?", so I prepared one!

650
00:44:15,204 --> 00:44:17,364
ナブナさんの「メリュー」！
n-buna-san's "Meryuu"!

651
00:44:17,684 --> 00:44:22,564
ナブナさんはあれだね、ヨルシカとかをやっ、の曲を作ってらっしゃる方？
n-buna-san is, you know, the person who creates songs for Yorushika.

652
00:44:22,784 --> 00:44:27,264
ヨルシカを始める前のボカロ名義？と言うのかな？の、
His Vocaloid alias, I guess you'd call it, from before starting Yorushika...

653
00:44:29,464 --> 00:44:32,464
曲ですね！そうなっちゃ！歌うのじゃー！
...it's his song! Indeed! Let's sing!

654
00:44:34,084 --> 00:44:36,484
今んとこ全部知らない？あ、そう、この歌枠はね、
"I don't know any of them so far"? Ah, yeah, this singing stream...

655
00:44:36,864 --> 00:44:42,564
いつもは結構おぬしらがわかるめの曲をいっぱい用意してくるんじゃけど、今日はかなり
Usually, I prepare plenty of songs that you guys would recognize, but today...

656
00:44:42,764 --> 00:44:46,064
漏れが、漏れ、漏れとか言っちゃった。
..."More-"... "More"? Did I really just say "more"?!

657
00:44:46,364 --> 00:44:49,264
わしが「歌いてえ！」って思ったのを、
...songs that I just really wanted to sing,

658
00:44:49,564 --> 00:44:55,764
ちょっと、だいぶ、だいぶ自己、自己満足的なところありを用意してきました。
so I put together a list that's pretty heavily driven by my own self-indulgence.

659
00:44:56,904 --> 00:45:00,064
から、あの、何だろう、知ってくれる
So, um, how should I put it... Getting to know...

660
00:45:00,072 --> 00:45:02,112
きっかけになるといいな
I hope it serves as a good trigger...

661
00:45:02,202 --> 00:45:04,472
って思いましたのじゃ！よいしょ！
...is what I thought-noja! Yoisho!

662
00:45:05,172 --> 00:45:09,022
それでは歌いますのじゃー！よいしょー！
Well then, I'm going to sing! Here we go!

663
00:45:09,752 --> 00:45:11,022
いけるか？
Ready to go?

664
00:45:11,922 --> 00:45:14,372
ん？ん。
Hm? Mhm.

665
00:45:15,892 --> 00:45:20,572
[Title: メリュー / n-buna / 作詞・作曲 n-buna]
[Title: Meryuu / n-buna / Lyrics & Music: n-buna]

666
00:45:27,202 --> 00:45:34,272
夕陽が落ちる様に
As the evening sun sets,

667
00:45:34,352 --> 00:45:41,472
胸が染まるので
my chest is dyed with color, so

668
00:45:42,022 --> 00:45:48,952
耳鳴りのような
like ringing in my ears,

669
00:45:49,192 --> 00:45:55,892
鼓動を隠して
I conceal my heartbeat.

670
00:45:56,312 --> 00:45:59,672
バスに乗った僕は言う
Boarding the bus, I say,

671
00:45:59,922 --> 00:46:03,812
君は灰になって征く
"You are turning to ashes and fading away."

672
00:46:04,212 --> 00:46:08,592
例えばこんな言葉さえ
If even words like this,

673
00:46:08,692 --> 00:46:11,972
失う言葉が僕に言えたら
words I'm losing, could be spoken by me...

674
00:46:12,092 --> 00:46:18,732
灯籠の咲く星の海に心臓を投げたのだ
Into the sea of stars where lanterns bloom, I threw my heart.

675
00:46:19,122 --> 00:46:26,612
もう声も出ない それは僕じゃどうしようもなかったのだ
My voice won't come out anymore; there was nothing I could do about it.

676
00:46:41,122 --> 00:46:48,132
悲しくもないし
I'm not sad,

677
00:46:48,472 --> 00:46:55,332
苦しくもないのに
nor am I suffering, and yet

678
00:46:55,772 --> 00:47:02,892
辛いと思うだけ
I only feel it's painful,

679
00:47:03,212 --> 00:47:10,332
辛いと思うだけ
I only feel it's painful.

680
00:47:10,672 --> 00:47:14,152
古びたバス停の端
At the edge of the worn-out bus stop,

681
00:47:14,352 --> 00:47:17,752
傘を持った僕がいる
there I stand holding an umbrella.

682
00:47:17,952 --> 00:47:22,572
今でさえ埃を被った
Even now, into the dusty

683
00:47:22,672 --> 00:47:25,612
夜空の隅に足はつくのに
corners of the night sky, my feet touch down, and yet...

684
00:47:25,872 --> 00:47:30,492
心臓が痛いから死んだふりの
Because my heart aches, playing dead,

685
00:47:30,652 --> 00:47:33,292
毎日を見なよ
just look at my every day.

686
00:47:33,392 --> 00:47:40,132
もういっそ死のうと思えたなら僕は楽だったのだ
If I could have just thought I'd rather die, I would have been at peace.

687
00:47:55,572 --> 00:48:02,772
どうせ死ぬくせに 辛いなんておかしいじゃないか
When I'm going to die anyway, isn't it ridiculous to say it's painful?

688
00:48:03,112 --> 00:48:10,892
どうせ死ぬくせに 辛いなんて
When I'm going to die anyway, to say it's painful...

689
00:48:11,092 --> 00:48:14,372
あぁ...
Ah...

690
00:48:14,952 --> 00:48:22,632
だから愛せない こんな世界の色に僕の唄を混ぜて
That's why, unable to love it, mixing my song into the colors of such a world,

691
00:48:22,912 --> 00:48:30,532
もうどうにかしたいと思うくせに 僕はどうもしないままで
even while wanting to do something about it, I remain doing nothing.

692
00:48:32,512 --> 00:48:41,012
あぁ、灯籠の咲く星の海に心臓を投げたのだ
Ah, into the sea of stars where lanterns bloom, I threw my heart.

693
00:48:41,352 --> 00:48:47,412
もう声も出ないから 死んだふりなんてどうもなかったのに
Since my voice won't come out anymore, playing dead was nothing at all,

694
00:48:47,552 --> 00:48:52,012
僕もきっとこうで良かったのに
and I'm sure it would have been fine for me to be like this, but

695
00:48:52,132 --> 00:48:56,952
君がずっと遠く笑ったのだ
you just kept smiling far away.

696
00:49:01,952 --> 00:49:06,172
メリューでしたのじゃ〜
That was "Meryuu"-noja~

697
00:49:08,992 --> 00:49:14,122
なんか、前回わしが歌枠やったときに、
You know, the last time I did a singing stream,

698
00:49:14,932 --> 00:49:19,322
すごいアップテンポなものが多くて、
there were so many really upbeat songs,

699
00:49:20,722 --> 00:49:26,612
アップテンポなものがめちゃくちゃ多かったから、ちょっとしっとりさせるかと思って。
since there were crazy amounts of upbeat tracks, I thought I'd tone things down a bit.

700
00:49:27,872 --> 00:49:33,492
「ちょっと、ちょっとしっとりめもお主ら欲しいんじゃないの〜？」って。
Like, "Don't you guys want something a little more mellow too~?"

701
00:49:34,972 --> 00:49:37,122
うん。そう、ボカロ多めだったから。
Yeah. Right, since there was a lot of Vocaloid rock.

702
00:49:37,372 --> 00:49:41,322
「しっとりも欲しいんじゃないのお主ら〜？」って思ったのじゃ。うん。
"Don't you guys want something mellow too~?" is what I thought-noja. Mhm.

703
00:49:41,992 --> 00:49:43,122
でも、
But...

704
00:49:43,972 --> 00:49:49,152
でも、わしがお主らをただしっとりさせるわけなくて、ワロタ。
But of course there's no way I'd just let you guys stay mellow, lol.

705
00:49:49,322 --> 00:49:52,552
しっとりたださせているつもりももちろんなく、
And of course I have no intention of just keeping it mellow,

706
00:49:52,812 --> 00:49:55,292
そろそろいいですか？暴れて。
so is it about time? Can I go wild?

707
00:49:55,872 --> 00:49:59,872
そろそろ、そろそろ暴れていいですか？
Is it about time... is it about time for me to go wild?

708
00:50:03,530 --> 00:50:07,880
そろそろお主らも、わしが暴れてるとこ見たいでしょ？
You folks probably want to see me go wild by now, right?

709
00:50:08,780 --> 00:50:10,280
ん。
Mhm.

710
00:50:11,780 --> 00:50:13,480
暴れたいなと思って。
I really felt like cutting loose.

711
00:50:14,380 --> 00:50:17,580
いやねー、ずっと好きって言ってたからねー。
Well, you see, I've always said how much I love it,

712
00:50:18,580 --> 00:50:22,380
なんか、聴きたかった人多いんじゃないかなーって思って。
so I figured there'd be a lot of people who wanted to hear it.

713
00:50:23,280 --> 00:50:27,580
え、でも、やっぱ好きなのと上手に歌えるのは違うんじゃよ。
But really, loving a song and singing it well are two completely different things!

714
00:50:27,780 --> 00:50:31,080
なんか、わかるじゃろ？お主らカラオケとかでさ、好きな曲歌ってもさ、
You know what I mean, right? When you go to karaoke and sing your favorite songs...

715
00:50:31,280 --> 00:50:32,980
なかなかさー、
it's often like...

716
00:50:33,280 --> 00:50:37,080
あのー、「いや、難しいな、この曲！好きなんだけどなー！」みたいな。
"Man, this song is so hard! Even though I love it so much!"

717
00:50:37,880 --> 00:50:39,980
うん、あるじゃろ？
You get that too, right?

718
00:50:40,480 --> 00:50:42,080
あると思うのですが、
I'm sure you do,

719
00:50:42,380 --> 00:50:48,080
ちょっとあのー、こんだけ言ってて、ちょっと触れないわけにはいかないなと思って持ってきました。
but after talking about it this much, I felt like I couldn't just ignore it, so I brought it along today!

720
00:50:48,380 --> 00:50:49,880
でででででで。
Ta-da-da-da-da!

721
00:50:50,580 --> 00:50:56,580
えっーと、あの、わしが自己紹介動画とか、いろんなところで、
Um, so in my introduction video and lots of other places,

722
00:50:56,780 --> 00:51:03,580
あの、「SAKKAKU CRAFT」っていうアルバムが好き、好きって話をずっとしておりまして。
I've constantly been talking about how much I love the album "SAKKAKU CRAFT."

723
00:51:04,280 --> 00:51:07,580
うん、「SAKKAKU CRAFT」が好きって話をずーっとしてたんじゃけど、
Yeah, I kept going on and on about loving "SAKKAKU CRAFT," but...

724
00:51:07,780 --> 00:51:10,580
ちょ、曲がむずすぎて、
the songs are just way too hard,

725
00:51:10,780 --> 00:51:19,580
曲がむずすぎて、ちょ、デビューして直後に、ちょっとムズい曲を歌って振り回されてるのを、ちょっと見せるのはちょっと申し訳ないなと思い、
they're so hard that right after debuting, I felt bad about showing myself struggling and getting totally overwhelmed by such difficult songs...

726
00:51:19,780 --> 00:51:23,580
うん。ちょ、申し訳ないなと思い、そう、ちょ、やっぱ難しい曲ってさ、
Yeah, I felt bad, and you know, with difficult songs...

727
00:51:23,780 --> 00:51:27,080
あの、歌ってみたとかだったらまだしもさ、生でさ、
In a recorded cover video, maybe it's fine, but singing live...

728
00:51:27,280 --> 00:51:31,580
難しい曲を歌うと結構、なんじゃろ、聴いてて不安になるというかさ。
when you sing a really hard song live, it kind of makes listeners feel uneasy, you know?

729
00:51:32,080 --> 00:51:36,580
「歌枠だし、こんなもんか、クオリティ」ってなっちゃうじゃろ？
Like, "Well, it's just a karaoke stream, I guess this is the quality," right?

730
00:51:36,780 --> 00:51:42,080
いや、それをデビューした直後にやると良くないかなと思ったけど、まあ流石にもうデビューして2ヶ月！
So I thought doing that right after debut wouldn't look good, but now it's already been two months!

731
00:51:42,280 --> 00:51:51,080
2ヶ月経って、まあここまで今わしのことを見てくれてる、あの人間たちは、ちょっとめらちゃんのことが大好き！なんじゃないの、お主ら？うん。
After two months, the humans who are still watching me this far must really love Mela-chan! Am I right? Mhm!

732
00:51:52,080 --> 00:52:02,080
お主らめらちゃんのこと大好きじゃから、まあ多少の難しさには目を瞑ってくれるかなと、ちょっと甘え...甘え、甘えておりますのじゃ。
Since you guys love Mela-chan so much, I figured you'd turn a blind eye to a few rough spots... so I'm depending on your kindness here!

733
00:52:03,080 --> 00:52:11,580
甘えておりまして、まあだから、まあ難しいけど好きな曲を歌っちゃおうかな、カラオケだし、と思って。
Yes, I'm spoiling myself! So I figured, even though it's hard, why not sing a song I love since it's karaoke?

734
00:52:11,880 --> 00:52:15,580
うん。歌わせていただきましのじゃー！
Yep! So I'm gonna go ahead and sing it!

735
00:52:16,280 --> 00:52:17,080
うん。
Mhm.

736
00:52:17,580 --> 00:52:22,080
ちなみに「SAKKAKU CRAFT」の中で何であのアノニマスファンファーレ持ってきたかと言うと、
By the way, as for why I chose "Anonymous Fanfare" from "SAKKAKU CRAFT"...

737
00:52:22,380 --> 00:52:30,080
なんか「SAKKAKU CRAFT」を「SAKKAKU CRAFT」たらしめる、な、なんじゃ、なんじゃろうな。いや全部、全部好きなんじゃ、もちろんね。全部好きだし、好きなんじゃが、
It's kind of what makes "SAKKAKU CRAFT" truly "SAKKAKU CRAFT"... how should I put it? I mean, of course I love all the songs! I love every single one, but...

738
00:52:31,080 --> 00:52:35,880
「SAKKAKU CRAFT」の顔だと思ってる、勝手に。
In my mind, I personally feel it's the signature track of "SAKKAKU CRAFT."

739
00:52:36,580 --> 00:52:43,880
なんか、あのツミキさんのボカロックの、すべて、すべて、すべてある！
Like, it has everything, everything, absolutely everything of Tsumiki-san's Voca-rock!

740
00:52:44,080 --> 00:52:49,080
ガチで「アノニマスファンファーレ」って、完、完全、完全の曲だと思ってて。
Seriously, I consider "Anonymous Fanfare" to be a complete, absolute masterpiece.

741
00:52:49,280 --> 00:52:50,080
そう。
Yeah.

742
00:52:50,280 --> 00:52:54,080
一番、一番完全ボカロックだと思ってるから。
Because I consider it the pinnacle of pure Voca-rock.

743
00:52:54,580 --> 00:52:58,580
完全ボカロックと思って選んで来ましたのじゃ。
Believing it's the ultimate Voca-rock song, that's why I picked it!

744
00:52:59,080 --> 00:53:02,580
のじゃ歌うのじゃー！
Now I shall sing it!

745
00:53:02,580 --> 00:53:07,580
早口になると声のトーンガチで変わる。やばいオタクなのバレちゃう。やめて！やめてほしいのじゃー！
When I talk fast, my tone of voice completely changes. Oh no, my nerdiness is showing! Stop! Please don't notice!

746
00:53:08,080 --> 00:53:12,880
可愛いと思われたいのにオタクくんなのバレちゃうのじゃー！
I want to be thought of as cute, but my inner otaku is totally exposed!

747
00:53:13,280 --> 00:53:16,880
それでは、歌うのじゃー！
Well then, I shall sing!

748
00:53:17,080 --> 00:53:18,480
頑張れ、わし！
Do your best, me!

749
00:53:18,580 --> 00:53:20,080
頑張れ、わし！
You can do this, me!

750
00:53:20,080 --> 00:53:22,080
めらちゃん大好きありがとう。
Thank you for all the "I love you, Mela-chan"s!

751
00:53:23,080 --> 00:53:27,580
[Title: アノニマスファンファーレ / ツミキ]
[Title: Anonymous Fanfare / Tsumiki]

752
00:53:30,080 --> 00:53:32,080
1, 2, 3, 4!

753
00:53:40,080 --> 00:53:43,780
たった、たた、たた、たた、たた、たた。
Ta-tta, ta-ta, ta-ta, ta-ta, ta-ta, ta-ta!

754
00:53:48,880 --> 00:53:52,580
(音声点検) 訊こえるか、僕の存在証明讃歌が。
(Voice Check) Can you hear it? My hymn proving my existence.

755
00:53:52,680 --> 00:53:57,680
師走の崩落は、カフスの裡面二つが喰って死んだ。
The December collapse, the two inside cuffs devoured it and died.

756
00:53:57,780 --> 00:54:02,080
ねえ僕は如何だ、如何様か。此れは電光朝露のゲイムだ。
Hey, how am I, what kind of fake am I? This is a game of fleeting morning dew.

757
00:54:02,380 --> 00:54:06,880
欲張って頬張ったフラクタルは、腐った様だった。た、た、た、た。
The fractal I greedily stuffed into my cheeks seemed to have rotted. Ta, ta, ta, ta.

758
00:54:06,980 --> 00:54:11,280
宙に舞って銃を持って、もう目が廻って仕舞うわ！ブレイクダウン。
Dancing in midair, holding a gun, my head is spinning already! Breakdown.

759
00:54:11,380 --> 00:54:15,580
僕のせいと、疑っているのは誰？誰？
Who is doubting that it's my fault? Who? Who?

760
00:54:15,780 --> 00:54:20,080
哀しくなって、言葉を売って、呼吸と二人法師になって、
Growing sad, selling my words, becoming a pair with my own breathing,

761
00:54:20,180 --> 00:54:24,480
最終回迄僕はずっと、夢の中。
all the way until the finale, I'm forever inside a dream.

762
00:54:24,480 --> 00:54:28,480
声を涸らして、愛を謳って、結末を待っている。
With my voice hoarse, singing of love, I wait for the conclusion.

763
00:54:28,580 --> 00:54:34,580
さらば！絶望的なハッピーエンド、クラップハンズなど必要無い、無い、無いわ！
Farewell! To this despairing happy ending, there's no need, no need, no need for clap hands!

764
00:54:41,280 --> 00:54:43,080
息できるところ短すぎん！？
The time to breathe is way too short, isn't it?!

765
00:54:51,880 --> 00:54:56,580
今に、ステップイントウ！踵鳴らす僕は二十三、時計と愛。
Soon enough, step into! Ringing my heels, I'm twenty-three, with a clock and love.

766
00:54:56,780 --> 00:55:00,080
匿名の音楽は、肥育の外連一つを孕んで飛んだ。
The anonymous music, bound for a fertile journey, took flight conceiving a single seed.

767
00:55:00,088 --> 00:55:02,238
孕んで飛んだ 方や僕は如何だ、如何様か。
...pregnant with pretense, it flew off. On the other hand, what am I? What kind of fraud is this?

768
00:55:02,288 --> 00:55:05,538
此れは半信半疑のルウルだ。
This is a rule of half-belief and doubt.

769
00:55:05,588 --> 00:55:09,738
散らかった芥は迷路の如く、僕を拘引して
The scattered refuse, like a labyrinth, hauled me away...

770
00:55:09,888 --> 00:55:12,738
点となって 線となって、嗚呼。
Becoming dots, becoming lines, ah...

771
00:55:12,788 --> 00:55:14,738
気が狂って終うわブレイクダウン。
I'm losing my mind—breakdown.

772
00:55:14,838 --> 00:55:18,338
全部全部 間違っているのは誰？ 誰？
All of it, every bit—who is in the wrong? Who?

773
00:55:18,438 --> 00:55:22,938
哀しくなって、言葉を売って、呼吸と二人法師になって、
Growing sorrowful, selling my words, becoming two solitaires with my breath...

774
00:55:23,038 --> 00:55:26,988
カーテンコールまで 秘密はきっと 夜の中。
Until the curtain call, the secret is surely in the night.

775
00:55:27,088 --> 00:55:30,988
目を瞑って、戯言を貼って、行場を探している
Closing my eyes, plastering nonsense, searching for a place to belong.

776
00:55:31,088 --> 00:55:34,038
さらば！ 絶望的なハッピーエンド
Farewell! To a desperate happy ending.

777
00:55:34,088 --> 00:55:37,388
クラップハンズなど いらない！ ない！ ない！
No need for clapping hands! None! None! None!

778
00:55:37,888 --> 00:55:41,588
ここ...ここガチで世界で一番いい。
Right here... this part is seriously the best in the world.

779
00:55:44,888 --> 00:55:46,488
マジでありがとう。
Seriously, thank you.

780
00:55:53,688 --> 00:55:57,988
名前を呼んで 僕を探して 帳で独り法師になって、
Call my name, search for me, left all alone behind the veil...

781
00:55:58,088 --> 00:56:02,588
エンドロールまで 記憶はずっと 帳の中。
Until the end roll, memories remain within the veil.

782
00:56:02,688 --> 00:56:09,138
忘れないで 思い出して 徒花が咲いている夜に 鳴り響くファンファーレ！
Don't forget, remember, on a night when phantom flowers bloom, a resounding fanfare rings out!

783
00:56:09,238 --> 00:56:13,738
哀しくなって 言葉を売って 呼吸と二人法師になって、
Growing sorrowful, selling my words, becoming two solitaires with my breath...

784
00:56:13,838 --> 00:56:17,938
最終回まで 僕は寸遠、夢の中。
Until the final episode, I am deep within a distant dream.

785
00:56:18,038 --> 00:56:22,038
声を枯らして 愛を歌って 結末を待っている
Exhausting my voice, singing of love, awaiting the conclusion.

786
00:56:22,088 --> 00:56:25,038
さらば！ 絶望的なハッピーエンド
Farewell! To a desperate happy ending.

787
00:56:25,138 --> 00:56:27,788
クラップハンズなど いらない！ ない！ ない！
No need for clapping hands! None! None! None!

788
00:56:27,888 --> 00:56:31,988
終生はその染み付いた 怨月と酷似している。
My whole life closely resembles that ingrained moon of grudge.

789
00:56:32,088 --> 00:56:36,488
三分と少しのエラーは 呼吸を開始した。
An error of just over three minutes began to breathe.

790
00:56:36,588 --> 00:56:40,588
たたたんたん たたたたたんたん
Ta-ta-tan-tan, ta-ta-ta-ta-tan-tan.

791
00:56:40,788 --> 00:56:43,088
ふふっ、はぁー... えーっと。
Hehe, whew... Umm...

792
00:56:43,788 --> 00:56:45,388
よいしょ。
There we go.

793
00:56:45,588 --> 00:56:49,988
のじゃー！『アノニマスファンファーレ』でしたのじゃー！
Noja~! That was "Anonymous Fanfare", noja~!

794
00:56:51,188 --> 00:56:55,288
あのねー、あの、お主ら気づいたと思うんだけどねー、
You know, um, I think you guys might have noticed, but...

795
00:56:55,388 --> 00:56:58,588
わしの好きなボカロ曲ってね、高くて早いのー！
the Vocaloid songs I like are really high and fast!

796
00:57:00,088 --> 00:57:05,988
わしがねー、ふふふ、わしが好きな曲ってね、高くて早いのじゃー！
The ones I, hehehe, the songs I like are just so high and fast, noja~!

797
00:57:06,088 --> 00:57:08,588
じゃから難しいのー！
That's why they're so hard!

798
00:57:09,888 --> 00:57:15,588
「歌ってみた」とかね、そう、あの、きれいにパッケージしてね、出したらいい感じなんじゃけど。
Like for a "song cover" video, yeah, if I packaged it up nicely and put it out, it'd probably turn out great, but...

799
00:57:16,588 --> 00:57:19,888
なかなか... なかなか難しい。
It's pretty... pretty tough.

800
00:57:19,988 --> 00:57:23,288
難しいが、ガチで好きなの。ガチで好きなの。
It's tough, but I seriously love it. I seriously love it!

801
00:57:25,488 --> 00:57:30,988
「めらちゃんの歌声で誕生日を迎えられて最高」本当？じゃあおめでとうの「アノニマスファンファーレ」！
"Welcoming my birthday with Mela-chan's singing is the best." Really? Then consider "Anonymous Fanfare" your birthday gift!

802
00:57:32,488 --> 00:57:35,888
お誕生日おめでとうなのじゃ！でも「クラップハンズなどいらない」って言ってるからな。
Happy birthday, noja! Though the song did say "No need for clapping hands."

803
00:57:35,988 --> 00:57:38,288
「いらない！ない！ない！」って言ってるからな。ふふふ。
It went, "No need, need, need!" after all. Hehehe.

804
00:57:38,488 --> 00:57:41,288
おめでとうなのじゃー！
Happy birthday, noja~!

805
00:57:41,388 --> 00:57:42,588
うん。
Yep.

806
00:57:43,288 --> 00:57:48,588
そう、「錯覚クラフト」ガチで全部...全部いい。全部良くて、全部大好き。
Yeah, "Sakkaku Craft" is seriously all... all good. Every song is great, and I love them all.

807
00:57:48,688 --> 00:57:53,388
わしの、あの、好きなアルバム一選。好きなアルバム一選なのじゃ。
It's my, um, top favorite album pick. One of my favorite albums of all time, noja.

808
00:57:53,488 --> 00:57:55,388
ガチで好き。
I seriously love it.

809
00:57:55,488 --> 00:58:00,888
あのー、今日は、あの、「アノニマスファンファーレ」入れたから、入れなかったけど、
Um, today, well, since I included "Anonymous Fanfare", I didn't add another, but...

810
00:58:02,588 --> 00:58:09,588
なんか「ノーメロ」さんとかもめっちゃ好きじゃから、いつか歌枠で歌いたいなーって思うのじゃ。
I also really love NOMELON NOLEMON, so I'd love to sing their songs on a singing stream sometime, noja.

811
00:58:09,688 --> 00:58:10,888
うん。
Yep.

812
00:58:11,688 --> 00:58:12,888
のじゃ。
Noja.

813
00:58:14,888 --> 00:58:19,488
そして、わし次何歌うつもり...あっ！やばい！ドーニソン来た！
And next, what was I planning to sing... Ah! Oh shoot! A pure anime song came!

814
00:58:19,588 --> 00:58:22,488
てかキャラソン来た！やばい、お主ら！お主らさー！
Or rather, a character song! Oh boy, you guys! Listen, you guys!

815
00:58:22,588 --> 00:58:25,088
お主ら本当にキャラソン歌いだしていい？
Can I really just go ahead and sing a character song?

816
00:58:25,188 --> 00:58:29,388
わしが...わしがキャラソン歌っても怒らない？
If I... if I sing a character song, you won't get mad?

817
00:58:30,388 --> 00:58:33,888
わしがキャラソン歌っても怒らない、お主ら？
You guys won't get mad at me if I sing a character song?

818
00:58:36,488 --> 00:58:39,288
今日、今日は好きな曲歌っていい？
Today—can I just sing songs that I like today?

819
00:58:40,888 --> 00:58:42,888
よし、それでは。
Alright, in that case...

820
00:58:44,888 --> 00:58:46,388
失礼して。
Pardon me.

821
00:58:46,588 --> 00:58:48,088
てぃてぃてぃてぃてぃ...
Ti-ti-ti-ti-ti...

822
00:58:48,388 --> 00:58:55,788
『殲琴・ダウルダブラ』を歌わせていただこうかなと思いますのじゃ。
I think I will sing "Senkin Daur da Bláo", noja.

823
00:58:56,488 --> 00:58:57,888
失礼して。
Pardon me.

824
00:58:58,288 --> 00:59:03,588
ふふふ、きゃ、キャラソン歌おうかなー。
Hehehe, time to sing a chara—character song~

825
00:59:04,188 --> 00:59:10,588
そう、『シンフォギア』の曲...キャラソンなのじゃ。
Yeah, it's a song from "Symphogear"... a character song, noja.

826
00:59:11,188 --> 00:59:11,988
うん。
Yep.

827
00:59:12,688 --> 00:59:15,688
歌わせていただきますのじゃー。
Allow me to sing it, noja~!

828
00:59:16,388 --> 00:59:19,488
よいしょ、BGMを切って...
Alright, turning off the BGM...

829
00:59:20,088 --> 00:59:21,888
よいしょー。
There we go.

830
00:59:22,488 --> 00:59:26,588
歌うのじゃー！
Here I go singing, noja~!

831
00:59:29,888 --> 00:59:31,788
かっこいいんじゃない？
Isn't it cool?

832
00:59:36,488 --> 00:59:40,888
ざー、ざー、がー
Zaa, zaa, gaa...

833
00:59:41,088 --> 00:59:47,888
じゅー、じゅー、じゅー、じゅー
Juu, juu, juu, juu...

834
00:59:53,288 --> 00:59:57,688
嗚呼、終焉への追走曲が薫る
Ah, the canon toward the end gives off its fragrance,

835
00:59:57,888 --> 01:00:00,184
殺戮の福音に血反吐と散れ
scattered with bloody vomit in the gospel of slaughter!

836
01:00:00,096 --> 01:00:02,596
殺戮の福音に血反吐と散れ
Scattering into blood and vomit upon the gospel of slaughter!

837
01:00:02,896 --> 01:00:06,796
微分子レベルまで解剖して
Dissecting down to the molecular level,

838
01:00:07,396 --> 01:00:11,896
反逆を永劫に断つ
I shall sever your rebellion for eternity!

839
01:00:13,096 --> 01:00:15,496
るLuリRぁ... 宇宙が傾き
Lu-lu-li-la... The universe tilts,

840
01:00:15,496 --> 01:00:17,896
RゥるRiラ... 太陽が凍る
Lu-lu-li-la... The sun freezes,

841
01:00:17,896 --> 01:00:21,596
Genocide & genocide

842
01:00:21,596 --> 01:00:24,396
ううう...
Ooh...

843
01:00:27,296 --> 01:00:29,896
血液一滴残らず
Without leaving a single drop of blood,

844
01:00:29,896 --> 01:00:32,696
憎悪と力で掻き毟る
I'll tear it all apart with hatred and force.

845
01:00:32,696 --> 01:00:37,696
震え怖じよ... 世界の崩れるLove song
Tremble and cower... at this love song of a collapsing world!

846
01:00:39,696 --> 01:00:44,696
奇跡など殺すと誓ったのだ
I swore I would slaughter all miracles!

847
01:00:44,696 --> 01:00:49,296
想い出など微塵も焼き消して
Burning away every last trace of memories,

848
01:00:49,296 --> 01:00:54,096
狂い酔えば柔きあの笑顔も
Intoxicated with madness, even those tender smiles,

849
01:00:54,096 --> 01:00:58,896
世界を壊す歌が忘却へと
This world-destroying song will cast into oblivion...

850
01:00:58,896 --> 01:01:03,996
愛など見えない 愛などわからぬ
I cannot see love, I do not understand love,

851
01:01:03,996 --> 01:01:08,496
愛など終わらせる
I will bring all love to an end!

852
01:01:16,096 --> 01:01:20,496
嗚呼、淡く優しく触れていた
Ah... Faintly and gently touching me,

853
01:01:20,496 --> 01:01:25,496
暖かく温もったあの掌
That warm, comforting palm of a hand...

854
01:01:25,496 --> 01:01:30,096
名前がもう思いだせやしない
I can't even remember the name anymore,

855
01:01:30,296 --> 01:01:34,096
枯れ果て尽くした心
In this completely withered heart.

856
01:01:35,096 --> 01:01:37,496
るLuリRぁ... 業火のレクイエム
Lu-lu-li-la... A requiem of hellfire,

857
01:01:37,496 --> 01:01:39,896
RゥるRiラ... くるりと踊るの
Lu-lu-li-la... Spinning and dancing,

858
01:01:39,896 --> 01:01:44,096
Genocide & genocide

859
01:01:44,096 --> 01:01:46,696
ううう...
Ooh...

860
01:01:49,696 --> 01:01:52,296
ドクンと脈打つすべてを
Everything that pulses with a heartbeat,

861
01:01:52,296 --> 01:01:55,096
生ある万物すべてを
All living things across creation,

862
01:01:55,096 --> 01:02:00,696
救済への階段から突キ落トセ...
Cast them down from the stairway to salvation...

863
01:02:02,096 --> 01:02:06,696
虚無こそが安寧の楽園と
That nothingness is the peaceful paradise,

864
01:02:06,796 --> 01:02:11,696
信ずこと以外に何があるか?
What else is there to believe in besides that?

865
01:02:11,896 --> 01:02:16,496
万象の摂理を暴き謳う
Laying bare and singing the providence of all things,

866
01:02:16,596 --> 01:02:21,696
0と1に鎮座した我が音楽
My music enshrined in zeroes and ones!

867
01:02:21,896 --> 01:02:26,696
愛など嬲ろう 愛など躙ろう
Let us toy with love! Let us trample on love!

868
01:02:26,696 --> 01:02:31,296
愛した... 購いを
For the atonement... of what I loved...

869
01:02:40,896 --> 01:02:42,496
まじかっこいい
This is so cool!

870
01:03:07,296 --> 01:03:09,796
るLuリRぁ... 消えてく... 絶えてく...
Lu-lu-li-la... Fading away... Dying out...

871
01:03:09,796 --> 01:03:12,396
RゥるRiラ... 歿してく... 死んでく...
Lu-lu-li-la... Perishing... Dying...

872
01:03:12,396 --> 01:03:16,496
Genocide & genocide

873
01:03:16,496 --> 01:03:18,896
ううう...
Ooh...

874
01:03:21,896 --> 01:03:24,596
涙の一滴残らず
Wringing out every last drop of tears,

875
01:03:24,596 --> 01:03:27,296
搾った怒号のカタストローフ
A catastrophe of wrung-out roaring cries!

876
01:03:27,296 --> 01:03:32,696
根底から完全否定シテ燃ヤス
Completely rejecting and burning it down from the foundation!

877
01:03:35,296 --> 01:03:40,096
奇跡など殺すと誓ったのだ
I swore I would slaughter all miracles!

878
01:03:40,296 --> 01:03:44,896
想い出など微塵も焼き消して
Burning away every last trace of memories,

879
01:03:44,896 --> 01:03:49,596
狂い酔えば柔きあの笑顔も
Intoxicated with madness, even those tender smiles,

880
01:03:49,596 --> 01:03:54,496
世界を壊す歌が忘却へと
This world-destroying song will cast into oblivion!

881
01:03:54,696 --> 01:03:59,696
愛していた日々 愛したあの日々
The days I loved... Those days I cherished...

882
01:03:59,696 --> 01:04:04,596
愛故... 永眠らせる
Out of love... I shall put you to eternal rest!

883
01:04:15,896 --> 01:04:18,296
のじゃ〜！
Noja~!

884
01:04:18,596 --> 01:04:22,596
『殲琴・ダウルダブラ』でしたのじゃ〜！
That was "Senkin Daur da Bláo", noja~!

885
01:04:23,296 --> 01:04:25,296
コメントでバレてる。
The comments saw right through me.

886
01:04:25,496 --> 01:04:28,096
キャラソン歌うとき、あちちめらがキャラソン歌うとき...
Whenever I sing character songs, whenever Achichi Mela sings character songs...

887
01:04:28,096 --> 01:04:33,496
歌い方を寄せてる...寄せようと頑張ってることがバレているのじゃ。
Everyone always notices how hard I try to mimic the original character's singing style, noja!

888
01:04:34,096 --> 01:04:36,496
バレてる。
Busted.

889
01:04:38,296 --> 01:04:40,496
うん、すごいねー。
Yeah, you guys are sharp!

890
01:04:40,696 --> 01:04:44,696
なんかね、シンフォギアねー、キャラソンかっこいい系めちゃくちゃ多くてねー。
Like, Symphogear has so many incredibly cool character songs.

891
01:04:44,696 --> 01:04:47,496
すごい好きなんだよんなー。
I really, really love them.

892
01:04:47,896 --> 01:04:52,496
そう、キャラソンというか、劇...劇中歌？
Yeah, or rather than character songs, insert... insert songs?

893
01:04:53,096 --> 01:04:56,296
なんか、わしの認識なんじゃけど、あのー...
Well, this is just how I see it, but, um...

894
01:04:56,896 --> 01:04:58,596
なんじゃろな...
How should I put it...

895
01:05:00,104 --> 01:05:02,904
オープニング、エンディングがアニソンで、
Anisongs are the openings and endings,

896
01:05:02,904 --> 01:05:09,604
それ以外のCV、キャラクターボイスの方が歌ってらっしゃるのが...
while songs sung by the voice cast, the character voices, are...

897
01:05:11,904 --> 01:05:13,204
キャラソン。
character songs.

898
01:05:13,304 --> 01:05:15,904
何？高くつくぜ俺の歌は？
What's that? "My song doesn't come cheap"?

899
01:05:19,504 --> 01:05:20,204
うん。
Yeah.

900
01:05:20,504 --> 01:05:25,904
そうそうそうそう。テーマ的にもね、あの、なんじゃろうな...
Right, right, right. In terms of themes too, well, how do I put it...

901
01:05:26,904 --> 01:05:28,504
高いんじゃよね。
it's pretty steep.

902
01:05:30,304 --> 01:05:33,304
そう、高いから...
Yeah, since it's up there...

903
01:05:36,504 --> 01:05:37,504
のじゃ。
noja.

904
01:05:40,104 --> 01:05:44,304
わし的には、声優さんが歌ったらキャラソン。
In my book, if a voice actor sings it, it's a character song.

905
01:05:44,904 --> 01:05:46,104
うん。
Yeah.

906
01:05:46,904 --> 01:05:47,804
そう。
Right.

907
01:05:48,104 --> 01:05:50,604
キャラソンめっちゃ好きなんじゃよね。
I just love character songs so much.

908
01:05:50,604 --> 01:05:53,704
なんかね、わしね、あの、なんじゃろうな...
Like, for me, well, how should I put it...

909
01:05:56,604 --> 01:06:02,104
あの、もうサブスクとかにもリリースされて、なんかブルーレイにしかついてこないさ、キャラソンとかあるじゃん。
Some character songs aren't on streaming and only come bundled with Blu-rays, right?

910
01:06:02,104 --> 01:06:05,204
なんか、キャラソンがめちゃくちゃ好きでさ。
Like, I just love character songs crazy amounts.

911
01:06:05,404 --> 01:06:08,904
そう、キャラソンを聴くのがめちゃくちゃ好きでさ。
Yeah, I totally love listening to character songs.

912
01:06:10,604 --> 01:06:15,004
だからその、いろんなアニメのキャラソンで好きなの、めちゃくちゃいっぱいあるんじゃけど...
So there are tons of character songs from all kinds of anime that I love, but...

913
01:06:15,604 --> 01:06:21,104
だいたいでキャラソンはね、あの、カラオケに入ってないことが多いんだよな。
character songs usually aren't available in karaoke catalogs.

914
01:06:21,604 --> 01:06:23,804
入ってないことが多いんだよな。
So many of them just aren't there.

915
01:06:23,804 --> 01:06:29,104
だから、歌いたくても歌えないみたいなことが、結構あるんだよな。
So it happens pretty often where I want to sing one, but I can't.

916
01:06:29,904 --> 01:06:33,504
確かに最近はもうキャラソンの文化があんまないか。
It's true that lately the whole character song culture isn't as big anymore.

917
01:06:33,504 --> 01:06:35,104
悲しい話なのじゃ。
It's quite sad, noja.

918
01:06:35,104 --> 01:06:35,804
うん。
Yeah.

919
01:06:35,804 --> 01:06:40,504
え、そう、ごちうさとか、そうそうそう。わしあれ好き、「魔女っ娘ラビュッティー」の好き。
Oh, yeah, like GochiUsa! Right, right. I love that one, "Majokko La-Beau-Tea".

920
01:06:41,604 --> 01:06:43,104
そうそうそう。
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

921
01:06:44,904 --> 01:06:49,904
え、そう、シンフォギアのさ、特典に入ってるのとかもあるよ、あるよね。そうそうそうそう。
Oh, yeah, Symphogear also has bonus tracks on the discs, right? Totally.

922
01:06:54,704 --> 01:07:00,104
じゃからね、いっぱいね、あのね、今後ね、アニソンをね、歌いたい。ちょっとずつね。
That's why I want to sing tons of anisongs in the future, bit by bit.

923
01:07:00,104 --> 01:07:04,704
あの全曲キャラソンの歌枠だと大変じゃからね。あの、なんじゃろ...
An all-character-song stream would be rough, so, like...

924
01:07:05,704 --> 01:07:13,704
多くの中の1つ、多くの中のね、1つをね、こう、そう、に入れていこうとね、思ってるのじゃ。
I'm thinking of weaving one in here and there among everything else, noja.

925
01:07:14,304 --> 01:07:20,204
そう、キャラソン、あの頃キャラソン作ってた人がね、今VTuberの楽曲作ってるんですよ。
Yeah, the people who were making character songs back then are composing for VTubers now!

926
01:07:20,204 --> 01:07:20,904
そう。
Yup.

927
01:07:21,104 --> 01:07:22,104
嬉しい。
That makes me so happy.

928
01:07:22,604 --> 01:07:25,604
神曲と、ガチで、ガチで神曲と思う。
Godly tracks! Honestly, I truly think they're godly tracks.

929
01:07:25,904 --> 01:07:28,504
か、神作家だらけで笑った。
It's hilarious how it's full of god-tier composers.

930
01:07:28,504 --> 01:07:34,604
VTuberの、VTuber楽曲の提供作家ガチ神作家だらけでヤバいのじゃ。
The composers providing songs for VTubers are seriously all god-tier, it's wild, noja.

931
01:07:36,604 --> 01:07:37,804
大好きなんじゃ。
I love it so much.

932
01:07:38,904 --> 01:07:41,604
「いつか作ってもらいたい」え、作ってもらいたいな。
"I hope you get one written for you someday." Oh, I'd love that!

933
01:07:41,604 --> 01:07:46,404
わしも、いやわしガチでさ、あのもうこんだけ見とれば、
Honestly, if you guys have been watching this much,

934
01:07:46,404 --> 01:07:49,104
さ、さすがにそろそろ皆様お気づきかと思うんですけど、
you've probably noticed by now, but...

935
01:07:49,104 --> 01:07:53,704
さすがに皆様お気づきかと思うんですけど、熱千めら、実は曲が好きで...
As you've probably noticed by now, Achichi Mela actually loves music...

936
01:07:54,104 --> 01:07:57,604
まだ気づいてない人あんまりいないかなと思うんじゃが、
I doubt there's anyone who hasn't realized yet,

937
01:07:57,604 --> 01:08:01,004
実は熱千めら、曲が好きで...
but Achichi Mela actually really loves music...

938
01:08:02,804 --> 01:08:05,604
実はね、実は。
Surprising, right? Seriously!

939
01:08:05,604 --> 01:08:07,104
実はね、そう。
Surprising, yeah.

940
01:08:07,604 --> 01:08:10,104
かなり実は曲が好きだし、
Quite honestly, I love songs,

941
01:08:10,104 --> 01:08:13,104
ボカロPさんも好きだし、作家さんも好きだし。
and I love Vocaloid producers, and I love composers too.

942
01:08:13,604 --> 01:08:14,404
で...
And...

943
01:08:16,104 --> 01:08:21,104
じゃから、あの、熱千めらももちろんオリ曲いっぱい作りたい！
So, Achichi Mela obviously wants to make tons of original songs!

944
01:08:21,604 --> 01:08:24,104
オリ曲をいっぱい作りたい！
I want to make tons of originals!

945
01:08:24,104 --> 01:08:26,604
ライブとかもしたいけど、
Doing live concerts and stuff would be great too, but...

946
01:08:27,104 --> 01:08:29,004
正直ライブしたい...
Honestly, wanting to do a concert...

947
01:08:29,004 --> 01:08:32,504
もちろんその先にライブがあるのはすごい嬉しいんじゃが、
Of course, getting to hold a live concert after that would make me so happy,

948
01:08:32,504 --> 01:08:34,604
あの、曲をね、発注したい！
but I want to commission songs!

949
01:08:35,004 --> 01:08:42,104
好きな作家さんに、自分のオーダー、好きの、わしの考える最強の楽曲を作ってもらいたい。
I want to have my favorite composers write my dream, ultimate songs based on my requests!

950
01:08:44,304 --> 01:08:48,404
あるの、「こういう曲作りたいな」みたいなのがめちゃくちゃあって。
I have so many ideas like, "I want to create a song like this!"

951
01:08:48,404 --> 01:08:49,904
めちゃくちゃ、やっぱね、
So many! You know,

952
01:08:49,904 --> 01:08:55,104
いや、お主らもさ、オタクくんとしてこうさ、音楽を聴いてる中でさ、
while you guys are listening to music as fellow nerds,

953
01:08:55,104 --> 01:09:00,004
「うわ、この曲いいな。わしだったらこの曲はライブのセトリのこの辺に持ってくな」とか思いながら聴くじゃろ？
don't you think stuff like, "Whoa, this song is great. If it were me, I'd put it around here in a concert setlist"?

954
01:09:00,104 --> 01:09:05,604
お主ら、お主らさ、好きな曲とかをさ、自分別にライブしないのにセットリスト作ったりするじゃろ？
You guys, even though you aren't doing lives yourselves, you make setlists with your favorite tracks, right?

955
01:09:05,604 --> 01:09:09,604
好きな曲で。「あー、ちょっとこれはライブのこの辺に入れたら熱いですね」とか、
Like, "Man, throwing this into this spot in the live would be so hype,"

956
01:09:09,604 --> 01:09:12,904
「ダブルアンコールにこれ欲しいですね」とか考えるじゃろ？やるでしょ？
or "We definitely need this for the double encore!" You do that, don't you?

957
01:09:12,904 --> 01:09:13,904
やるじゃろ？
I know you do!

958
01:09:14,104 --> 01:09:16,904
「MIDとか」うわ、な、みたいな感じでわしは、
"Like in the mid-section..." Exactly! Just like that,

959
01:09:16,904 --> 01:09:21,604
曲を聴きながら、「うわ、このボカロPさんは...」ボカロPさんとか結構テイストがわかりやすいから、
while listening to songs, I go, "Whoa, this Vocaloid producer..." Since their style is usually easy to pick up on,

960
01:09:21,604 --> 01:09:27,604
「うわ、この人こういう系が得意だから、わしだったらこの人のこういう系が見たいな」みたいな。
I think, "Whoa, this person excels at this style, so personally I'd love to see this kind of track from them!"

961
01:09:28,104 --> 01:09:36,604
そう、まあだから、わしへの提供じゃなくても、その企画書を渡してそれをそのまま作って自分の曲として出していただいても構わない...
So, even if it's not provided to me, I'd gladly hand over a proposal and let them make it as their own song...

962
01:09:36,604 --> 01:09:38,604
もちろん構わないし、それですごい嬉しいのですよ。
Of course I wouldn't mind at all; that would make me super happy!

963
01:09:38,604 --> 01:09:42,604
ちょ、早口早口。のじゃのじゃのじゃ。のじゃ！
Fast talking, fast talking. Noja noja noja. Noja!

964
01:09:42,604 --> 01:09:45,104
いやまあ、何が言いたいかと言うと、
Well, what I really want to say is,

965
01:09:45,104 --> 01:09:52,604
あの、なんか曲を聴きながら、「うわ、この人はこういう曲が得意だから、わしこういうの頼みたいな」みたいなのがいっぱいあるの！
while listening to songs, I have so many thoughts like, "Whoa, they're so good at this kind of song, so I'd love to commission something like this!"

966
01:09:52,604 --> 01:09:54,104
「この人にはこれ頼みたい」
"I want to ask this person for this!"

967
01:09:54,104 --> 01:09:55,804
「この人にはこれ頼みたい」
"I want to ask that person for that!"

968
01:09:55,804 --> 01:09:58,604
「この人はこういうのが得意だから、こうしたら多分もっといいのができる」みたいなさ、
"Since they're great at this style, doing it like this would probably make it even better!"

969
01:09:58,604 --> 01:10:00,104
そういうのがめちゃくちゃ思いつくのじゃ。
Ideas like that just keep popping into my head, noja!

970
01:10:00,112 --> 01:10:01,312
そう
Right.

971
01:10:02,912 --> 01:10:04,712
じゃから...
So...

972
01:10:05,212 --> 01:10:10,612
まあまあまあ、だからやっぱこうね、いずれね、いっぱいオリ曲とかもね、出したいなって思ってるの！
Well, well, so that's why, eventually, I really want to release lots of original songs and stuff!

973
01:10:10,812 --> 01:10:13,312
頼みたいものがいっぱいなのじゃ！
There are so many people I want to commission!

974
01:10:13,512 --> 01:10:16,712
え、だって夢じゃない？夢じゃないか、おぬしら考えてみ？
I mean, isn't it the ultimate dream? Just think about it, guys!

975
01:10:16,712 --> 01:10:22,912
自分の好きなさ、自分の好きな作家さんにさ、自分がさ、好きなようにさ、発注できんだよ？
You get to commission your favorite composers and tell them exactly what you want!

976
01:10:22,912 --> 01:10:26,412
「こういう曲が作りたくて、こういう歌詞を入れたくて、こういうことをしたくて」みたいな、
"Like, 'I want to make this kind of song, with these lyrics, doing this kind of thing.'"

977
01:10:26,412 --> 01:10:30,612
「こういう、あの、編曲でお願いしたくて」みたいな、そういうのをさ、言えるのガチ、ガチで神でワロタ。
"Like, 'I'd like this kind of arrangement.' Being able to say all that is seriously god-tier, lol."

978
01:10:30,912 --> 01:10:37,812
なんかもう、「い、いいんですか？オ、オタク君の、僕の考える最強の〇〇を、あの、再現していただいていいのですか？」って思うんだけど。
I'd be like, "I-Is it really okay? Is it really okay for you to bring this otaku's ultimate dream concept to life?"

979
01:10:37,812 --> 01:10:41,112
ちょっと、ちょっと、ちょっとそれって... それってちょっと、なんか、
Like, wait, wait, wouldn't that be...

980
01:10:41,112 --> 01:10:45,412
あの、職権乱用オタク君すぎます？私利私欲オタク君すぎませんか？と思い、思いつつ...
like, abusing my power as an otaku? Isn't that indulging my own selfish otaku desires too much? But while I think that...

981
01:10:45,412 --> 01:10:48,612
思いつつ、わしそれなの！わしそれなのじゃ！
...that's just what I am! That's who I am!

982
01:10:48,612 --> 01:10:52,312
そう、だからガチで楽しみ！
Yeah, so I'm seriously looking forward to it!

983
01:10:52,312 --> 01:10:55,912
ガチでオリ曲出すの、ガチで楽しみなのじゃ。
Seriously, releasing original songs is something I'm super excited about.

984
01:10:56,112 --> 01:10:58,312
夢ある。超夢ある。
It's the dream. Such a dream.

985
01:10:59,112 --> 01:11:04,512
もう嬉しい。もう、こ、これ以上の喜びない、世界に、実は。
I'm so thrilled. Honestly, there's no greater joy in this world.

986
01:11:04,512 --> 01:11:08,612
実は、実はこれ以上の喜びって世界になくて。
Actually, there really is no greater joy in the whole world.

987
01:11:09,412 --> 01:11:12,612
そう、すっごい、すっごい楽しみなのじゃ。
Yeah, so I'm really, really looking forward to it.

988
01:11:15,712 --> 01:11:19,312
いや、そうそうそう。ホロ、ホロド... ホロドリです。
Yeah, that's right. Holo... HoloDori.

989
01:11:19,312 --> 01:11:21,912
ホロ... もちろんホロドリにも入りたいのじゃ。
Holo... Of course I want to be in HoloDori too!

990
01:11:21,912 --> 01:11:26,912
むしろホロドリとしても楽曲を出させていただきたいです。実装も、あの、くいっくいっくいっ、お待ちしておりますのじゃ。
In fact, I'd love to release songs as HoloDori as well. I'm eagerly waiting to be added, nudge nudge.

991
01:11:28,312 --> 01:11:32,312
そして、あと1曲用意してきたのおぬしら。
And I've prepared one more song for you all!

992
01:11:33,312 --> 01:11:36,512
あと1曲用意してきたの。まだまだ歌ってもいいが...
I prepared one more song. I could sing even more, though...

993
01:11:36,512 --> 01:11:44,112
なんかね、今日22時からの配信あったんだけどね、なくなったからね、まだまだ歌ってもいいのですが、とりあえずあと1曲だけPNG用意してきた。
I had a stream scheduled from 22:00 tonight, but it was canceled, so I could keep singing. But anyway, I only prepared one more PNG slide.

994
01:11:44,312 --> 01:11:46,012
10枚PNGに...
On my 10 PNGs...

995
01:11:46,712 --> 01:11:52,312
10枚PNGに用意してきた1曲があり、
I have that one song prepared on my 10 PNG slides,

996
01:11:53,512 --> 01:11:55,312
そう、あるので...
so...

997
01:11:56,712 --> 01:11:58,312
ど、どうじゃ？
What do you think?

998
01:11:58,512 --> 01:12:02,312
予想とかする？おぬしら、おぬしら予想とかしてみる？
Want to guess? Do you guys want to try guessing?

999
01:12:07,412 --> 01:12:10,412
ん？喉、喉は、喉はまだ大丈夫。
Hm? Throat? My throat is still fine.

1000
01:12:10,412 --> 01:12:12,812
今んとこ大丈夫だけど。
It's totally fine for now.

1001
01:12:14,112 --> 01:12:16,712
えっとな、あ、大喜利が始まった。えっとな、
Well, ah, the chat started making jokes. Um...

1002
01:12:16,712 --> 01:12:18,612
アニソンです！
It's an anime song!

1003
01:12:19,312 --> 01:12:22,512
アニソンであり、キャラソンです。
It's an anime song, and a character song.

1004
01:12:23,112 --> 01:12:24,612
キャラソンです。
A character song.

1005
01:12:25,412 --> 01:12:27,212
ボカロではありません。
It's not Vocaloid.

1006
01:12:27,612 --> 01:12:29,012
ボカロではありません。
It's not Vocaloid.

1007
01:12:29,412 --> 01:12:32,112
え、そして、え、デュエット曲です。
And, um, it's a duet song.

1008
01:12:33,112 --> 01:12:35,312
デュエット曲。
